/-! ## Uniqueness and the Bayes-plausible selector

The differentiability and genericity assumptions are bundled in
`MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable`:

* `v` is `C¹`, and satisfies the genericity condition that no two distinct points `x, y ∈ s.X`
  share a gradient (`∇v(x) = ∇v(y)`) and intercept (`v(x) − ∇v(x)·x = v(y) − ∇v(y)·y`) while the
  chord over `[x, y]` lies weakly above `v` (the `v_genericity` field below; this is stronger than,
  and not visibly equivalent to, "not affine on any line segment" outside one dimension);
* `μ₀` pushes forward through `m` to a measure absolutely continuous with respect to Lebesgue on
  `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)`.

The headline theorem `unique_optimal_joint_bayesPlausible` additionally requires, as separate
hypotheses on top of `MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable`:

* Lipschitzness of the moment coordinates (`MomentSetup.IsCoordLipschitz`);
* Lipschitzness, measurability, boundedness, and upper semicontinuity of `v`, together with
  measurability and upper semicontinuity of the composed value `μ ↦ v(E_μ[m])`;
* Lipschitzness of the posterior check (convex roof) of every Lipschitz price on `X`
  (`h_pcheck_lip`);
* an open-positive prior measure (`IsOpenPosMeasure`);
* density of the moment image in `X` (`s.X ⊆ closure (range m)`).

The surjectivity field `moment_surjOn_X` of `MomentSetup` (every `y ∈ X` is achievable as a
posterior moment) is also in force throughout.

Under these assumptions, the optimal joint is unique and the state space `Ω` decomposes into cells
`Ω_x = χ⁻¹({x})` (one for each `x ∈ S`) selected by a measurable map `χ : Ω → X`.  These cells are
convex in the classical interval setting `Ω = X`, but convexity is not expressible under the
present abstract hypotheses on `Ω`; see `BayesPlausibleSelector`.

The key objects are the **contact correspondence** `chi_corr v S ω` — the set of active points
`x ∈ S` realizing the tangent envelope `pStar v S ω` — and the **contact-set fiber**
`Gamma_x s v S x` — the set of `ω ∈ s.X` in contact with `x`.  By Rademacher's theorem and the
absolute-continuity hypothesis, `pStar v S` is differentiable at `μ₀ ∘ m⁻¹`-a.e. `ω`, and at each
such `ω` the genericity condition `v_genericity` forces `chi_corr v S ω` to be a singleton. -/

/-- Standing differentiability and genericity assumptions. -/
structure MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    (v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ) : Prop where
  /-- `v` is continuously differentiable. -/
  v_C1 : ContDiff ℝ 1 v
  /-- **Genericity hypothesis.**  No two distinct points `x, y ∈ s.X` simultaneously satisfy:

  * `∇v(x) = ∇v(y)`,
  * `v(x) − ∇v(x)·x = v(y) − ∇v(y)·y`, and
  * `t·v(x) + (1−t)·v(y) ≥ v(t·x + (1−t)·y)` for all `t ∈ [0, 1]`.

  This condition rules out non-singleton contact sets generated by distinct points with the same
  gradient and intercept. -/
  v_genericity : ∀ x ∈ s.X, ∀ y ∈ s.X, x ≠ y →
    fderiv ℝ v x = fderiv ℝ v y →
    v x - (fderiv ℝ v x) x = v y - (fderiv ℝ v y) y →
    ¬ ∀ t ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1,
        t * v x + (1 - t) * v y ≥ v (t • x + (1 - t) • y)
  /-- The prior pushed forward through the moment map `s.m : Ω → X` is absolutely continuous with
  respect to Lebesgue measure on `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)`.

  This is the standing absolute-continuity hypothesis to our setup with separate state space `Ω`
  and moment space `X = s.X`: Whenever `Ω = X` and `m = id` (the simplest setup), this reduces to
  `μ₀ ≪ Lebesgue` exactly.  In general it asks that the law of the moment `m(ω)` under `μ₀` has no
  atoms or singular components — the property Rademacher's theorem needs to push `pStar v S` to be
  a.e. differentiable under the pushforward. -/
  prior_pushforward_AC :
    (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m).AbsolutelyContinuous
      (MeasureTheory.volume : MeasureTheory.Measure (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))

/-- A *Bayes-plausible selector* for an active set `S ⊆ X`: A measurable cell-assignment
`χ : Ω → X` that maps `Ω` into `S` (a.s.) and satisfies the **Bayes-plausibility identity**: For
each `x ∈ S`, the prior restricted to `χ⁻¹({x})` integrates `m` to `x`-times-the-cell-mass.

The Bayes-plausibility identity is the integrated form of "the prior conditional on `χ⁻¹({x})` has
moment `x`".

The cells `χ⁻¹({x})` are the fibers of the optimal assignment.  In the classical statement of the
result (Dworczak–Kolotilin 2024, Theorem 7), where `Ω = X` is a real interval, these fibers are
*convex* — the optimum is convex-partitional.  That convexity cannot be *stated* here: The ambient
hypotheses on `Ω` are only topological / measurable / pseudometric, with no vector-space structure
in which to express convexity of subsets of `Ω`.  Hence this structure carries the measurable
selector and the Bayes-plausibility identity it satisfies, not a convexity field.  Strengthening to
an actual convex partition (adding vector-space structure on `Ω` and a `cells_convex` field) is
tracked as deferred work. -/
structure BayesPlausibleSelector (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    (S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) where
  /-- Cell-assignment function `χ : Ω → X`.  The cell of `x` is `χ⁻¹({x})`. -/
  chi : Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)
  /-- `χ` is measurable. -/
  chi_meas : Measurable chi
  /-- `χ` maps prior-a.e. into the active set `S`. -/
  chi_in_S_ae : ∀ᵐ ω ∂s.prior.toMeasure, chi ω ∈ S
  /-- **Bayes plausibility.**  For each `x ∈ S`, the integral of `m` over the prior restricted to
  `χ⁻¹({x})` equals `(prior-mass of cell)·x`. -/
  bayes_plausibility : ∀ x ∈ S,
    ∫ ω in chi ⁻¹' {x}, s.m ω ∂s.prior.toMeasure =
      (s.prior.toMeasure (chi ⁻¹' {x})).toReal • x

omit [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] in
/-- **Existence of optimal joint for moment persuasion.**

Under boundedness and upper semicontinuity of the value function, the supremum defining
`momentPrimal s v` is attained by some feasible joint `pi*`. -/
lemma exists_optimal_joint
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n) (hm_lip : s.IsCoordLipschitz)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ} {L : NNReal}
    (hv : LipschitzWith L (fun x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => v x))
    (hv_meas : Measurable v) (hv_bdd : ∃ M, ∀ x, |v x| ≤ M)
    (hv_usc : UpperSemicontinuous v)
    (hV_bdd : ∃ M, ∀ μ : ProbDist Ω, |s.composedValue v μ| ≤ M)
    (hV_usc : UpperSemicontinuous (s.composedValue v)) :
    ∃ pi ∈ feasibleJoint s, ∫ p, v p.1 ∂pi.toMeasure = momentPrimal s v := by
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ_feas, hτ_val⟩ :=
    Econlib.MechanismDesign.InformationDesign.Persuasion.Duality.primalAttainment
      hV_bdd hV_usc s.prior
  refine ⟨jointFromBayesian s τ, isFeasibleJoint_jointFromBayesian s hτ_feas, ?_⟩
  rw [integral_v_fst_jointFromBayesian s τ hv_meas hv_bdd, hτ_val,
    momentPrimal_eq_concaveClosure_composedValue s hm_lip hv hv_bdd hv_usc]

/-! ### Contact correspondence and contact set

`pStar v S` is the tangent-envelope candidate for an active set `S`.  We add the correspondence
`chi_corr` and the contact-set fiber `Gamma_x` used in the uniqueness analysis. -/

/-- **Contact correspondence.**

`chi_corr v S ω` is the set of active points `x ∈ S` realizing the upper envelope
`pStar v S ω = v(x) + (fderiv ℝ v x)(ω - x)`.  Under the standing regularity, optimality, density,
and differentiability hypotheses, this set is a singleton for prior-a.e. `ω`; that singleton is the
selector's cell map `χ : Ω → S★`. -/
def chi_corr
    (v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ)
    (S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))
    (ω : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) :
    Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) :=
  {x ∈ S | v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x) = pStar v S ω}

/-- **Contact-set fiber.**

For `x ∈ S`, `Gamma_x v S x` is the set of `ω ∈ s.X` such that `(x, ω)` lies on the contact set:
`pStar v S ω = v(x) + (fderiv ℝ v x)(ω - x)`.  Equivalently,
`ω ∈ Gamma_x v S x ↔ x ∈ chi_corr v S ω`.

Geometrically, `Γ_x` is the projection of the face of `epi(pStar)` exposed by the direction
`(-1, ∇v(x))`; the main fiber properties are compactness, convexity, and membership of the active
point. -/
def Gamma_x
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    (v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ)
    (S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))
    (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) :
    Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) :=
  {ω ∈ s.X | pStar v S ω = v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)}

/-- The graph `{(ω, x) : x ∈ chi_corr v S ω}` is closed in `ℝⁿ × ℝⁿ` whenever `v ∈ C¹`, `S` is
closed, and `pStar v S` is continuous.  Used to discharge the graph-regularity hypothesis of
`exists_measurable_selection_of_singleton_ae`. -/
lemma chi_corr_graph_isClosed
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS_closed : IsClosed S)
    (hpStar_cont : Continuous (pStar v S)) :
    IsClosed
      {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) |
        p.2 ∈ chi_corr v S p.1} := by
  have h_v_cont : Continuous v := hv_diff.continuous
  have h_fderiv_cont : Continuous (fderiv ℝ v) := hv_diff.continuous_fderiv one_ne_zero
  have h_snd_in_S :
      IsClosed
        {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) | p.2 ∈ S} :=
    hS_closed.preimage continuous_snd
  have h_lhs :
      Continuous fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) =>
        v p.2 + (fderiv ℝ v p.2) (p.1 - p.2) := by
    refine (h_v_cont.comp continuous_snd).add ?_
    exact (h_fderiv_cont.comp continuous_snd).clm_apply
      (continuous_fst.sub continuous_snd)
  have h_rhs :
      Continuous fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) =>
        pStar v S p.1 :=
    hpStar_cont.comp continuous_fst
  have h_eq :
      IsClosed
        {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) |
          v p.2 + (fderiv ℝ v p.2) (p.1 - p.2) = pStar v S p.1} :=
    isClosed_eq h_lhs h_rhs
  have h_set_eq :
      {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) |
          p.2 ∈ chi_corr v S p.1}
        = {p | p.2 ∈ S} ∩
            {p | v p.2 + (fderiv ℝ v p.2) (p.1 - p.2) = pStar v S p.1} := by
    ext p
    simp only [chi_corr, Set.mem_setOf_eq, Set.mem_inter_iff]
  rw [h_set_eq]
  exact h_snd_in_S.inter h_eq

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- The graph `{(x, ω) : ω ∈ Gamma_x s v S x}` is closed in `ℝⁿ × ℝⁿ` whenever `v ∈ C¹` and `s.X`
is closed (which it always is, being compact).  Used to discharge the closed-graph hypothesis of
the measurable Carathéodory selector in `Econlib.Math.Analysis.MeasurableCaratheodory`. -/
lemma Gamma_x_graph_isClosed (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    (S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))
    (hpStar_cont : Continuous (pStar v S)) :
    IsClosed
      {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) |
        p.2 ∈ Gamma_x s v S p.1} := by
  have h_v_cont : Continuous v := hv_diff.continuous
  have h_fderiv_cont : Continuous (fderiv ℝ v) := hv_diff.continuous_fderiv one_ne_zero
  have h_snd_in_X :
      IsClosed
        {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) | p.2 ∈ s.X} :=
    s.X_compact.isClosed.preimage continuous_snd
  have h_lhs :
      Continuous fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) =>
        pStar v S p.2 :=
    hpStar_cont.comp continuous_snd
  have h_rhs :
      Continuous fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) =>
        v p.1 + (fderiv ℝ v p.1) (p.2 - p.1) := by
    refine (h_v_cont.comp continuous_fst).add ?_
    exact (h_fderiv_cont.comp continuous_fst).clm_apply
      (continuous_snd.sub continuous_fst)
  have h_eq :
      IsClosed
        {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) |
          pStar v S p.2 = v p.1 + (fderiv ℝ v p.1) (p.2 - p.1)} :=
    isClosed_eq h_lhs h_rhs
  have h_set_eq :
      {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) |
          p.2 ∈ Gamma_x s v S p.1}
        = {p | p.2 ∈ s.X} ∩
            {p | pStar v S p.2 = v p.1 + (fderiv ℝ v p.1) (p.2 - p.1)} := by
    ext p
    simp only [Gamma_x, Set.mem_setOf_eq, Set.mem_inter_iff]
  rw [h_set_eq]
  exact h_snd_in_X.inter h_eq

/-! #### Contact-set calculus

The contact-set calculus relates differentiability of the envelope `pStar v S` to the geometry
of its contact fibers:

* `pStar` is differentiable at `ω ∈ int s.X` iff `{∇v(x) : x ∈ chi_corr v S ω}` is a singleton; in
  that case `∇(pStar v S) ω = ∇v(x)` for all `x ∈ chi_corr v S ω`.
* for `x ∈ S★`, `Γ_x` is compact convex with `x ∈ Γ_x`, and equals the argmin of
  `ω ↦ pStar v S ω - ⟨∇v(x), ω⟩` over `s.X`.
* three implications relate `Γ_x` and `Γ_y` via gradient equality and (relative-)interior
  intersection. -/

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- **Gradient identification.**

When `pStar v S` is differentiable at `ω ∈ int s.X` and `x ∈ chi_corr v S ω`, the Fréchet
derivative coincides with the derivative of `v` at `x`. -/
lemma fderiv_pStar_eq_fderiv_v_at_chi
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS : S ⊆ s.X)
    -- kept for the statement's contract (ω is an interior point); unused in this proof
    {ω : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (_hω : ω ∈ interior s.X)
    (h_diff : DifferentiableAt ℝ (pStar v S) ω)
    {x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (hx : x ∈ chi_corr v S ω) :
    fderiv ℝ (pStar v S) ω = fderiv ℝ v x := by
  obtain ⟨hxS, h_eq⟩ := hx
  have h_tangent_le : ∀ z, v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (z - x) ≤ pStar v S z := fun z =>
    le_csSup (pStar_image_bddAbove s hv_diff hS z) ⟨x, hxS, rfl⟩
  -- g(z) := pStar v S z - (v x + fderiv v x · (z - x)) is the tangent deficit; g ≥ 0 and g(ω) = 0.
  set g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ :=
    fun z => pStar v S z - (v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (z - x)) with hg_def
  have h_g_nonneg : ∀ z, 0 ≤ g z := fun z => sub_nonneg.mpr (h_tangent_le z)
  have h_g_zero_at_ω : g ω = 0 := by
    change pStar v S ω - (v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) = 0
    linarith [h_eq]
  have h_local_min : IsLocalMin g ω := by
    refine Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun z => ?_
    rw [h_g_zero_at_ω]; exact h_g_nonneg z
  have h_id_sub : HasFDerivAt (fun z : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => z - x)
      (ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) ω :=
    (hasFDerivAt_id ω).sub_const x
  have h_lin_deriv : HasFDerivAt (fun z : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) =>
        (fderiv ℝ v x) (z - x)) (fderiv ℝ v x) ω := by
    have h := (fderiv ℝ v x).hasFDerivAt.comp ω h_id_sub
    rw [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_id] at h
    exact h
  have h_tan_HasFDeriv :
      HasFDerivAt (fun z : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (z - x))
        (fderiv ℝ v x) ω :=
    h_lin_deriv.const_add (v x)
  have h_tan_diff :
      DifferentiableAt ℝ (fun z : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) =>
        v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (z - x)) ω :=
    h_tan_HasFDeriv.differentiableAt
  have h_tan_fderiv :
      fderiv ℝ (fun z : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (z - x)) ω =
        fderiv ℝ v x :=
    h_tan_HasFDeriv.fderiv
  have h_g_HasFDeriv :
      HasFDerivAt g (fderiv ℝ (pStar v S) ω - fderiv ℝ v x) ω :=
    h_diff.hasFDerivAt.sub h_tan_HasFDeriv
  have h_g_fderiv_eq :
      fderiv ℝ g ω = fderiv ℝ (pStar v S) ω - fderiv ℝ v x :=
    h_g_HasFDeriv.fderiv
  have h_g_fderiv_zero : fderiv ℝ g ω = 0 := h_local_min.fderiv_eq_zero
  rw [h_g_fderiv_eq] at h_g_fderiv_zero
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp h_g_fderiv_zero

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- If `pStar v S` is differentiable at `ω ∈ int s.X`, then all elements of the contact
correspondence share the same Fréchet derivative. -/
lemma fderiv_v_eq_of_chi_corr_at_diff
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS : S ⊆ s.X)
    {ω : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (hω : ω ∈ interior s.X)
    (h_diff : DifferentiableAt ℝ (pStar v S) ω)
    {x y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    (hx : x ∈ chi_corr v S ω) (hy : y ∈ chi_corr v S ω) :
    fderiv ℝ v x = fderiv ℝ v y :=
  (fderiv_pStar_eq_fderiv_v_at_chi s hv_diff hS hω h_diff hx).symm.trans
    (fderiv_pStar_eq_fderiv_v_at_chi s hv_diff hS hω h_diff hy)

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- If all contact points at `ω ∈ int s.X` have the same derivative of `v`, then `pStar v S` is
differentiable at `ω`.  The closedness of `S` ensures that the upper envelope attains its supremum
over `S`. -/
lemma pStar_differentiableAt_of_grad_singleton
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS : S ⊆ s.X) (hS_closed : IsClosed S)
    (hS_ne : S.Nonempty)
    {ω : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (hω : ω ∈ interior s.X)
    (h_grad_singleton : ∃ g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) →L[ℝ] ℝ,
      ∀ x ∈ chi_corr v S ω, fderiv ℝ v x = g) :
    DifferentiableAt ℝ (pStar v S) ω := by
  obtain ⟨g_clm, hg⟩ := h_grad_singleton
  have hS_compact : IsCompact S := s.X_compact.of_isClosed_subset hS_closed hS
  haveI : Nonempty ↥S := hS_ne.to_subtype
  haveI : CompactSpace ↥S := isCompact_iff_compactSpace.mp hS_compact
  have hv_cont : Continuous v := hv_diff.continuous
  have h_fderiv_cont : Continuous (fderiv ℝ v) := hv_diff.continuous_fderiv one_ne_zero
  -- fSub y z = v(z) + fderiv v z · (y - z) is the tangent of v at z evaluated at y.
  let fSub : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ↥S → ℝ := fun y z =>
    v z.1 + (fderiv ℝ v z.1) (y - z.1)
  let g_vec : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) := (InnerProductSpace.toDual ℝ _).symm g_clm
  let grad_fSub : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ↥S → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) := fun _ z =>
    (InnerProductSpace.toDual ℝ _).symm (fderiv ℝ v z.1)
  have h_fSub_cont : Continuous (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × ↥S => fSub p.1 p.2) := by
    refine (hv_cont.comp (continuous_subtype_val.comp continuous_snd)).add ?_
    exact Continuous.clm_apply
      (h_fderiv_cont.comp (continuous_subtype_val.comp continuous_snd))
      (continuous_fst.sub (continuous_subtype_val.comp continuous_snd))
  have h_cont : Danskin.ContinuousOnProd fSub (interior s.X) := h_fSub_cont.continuousOn
  have h_diff : ∀ z : ↥S, ∀ y ∈ interior s.X,
      HasGradientAt (fun w => fSub w z) (grad_fSub y z) y := by
    intro z y _hy
    change HasGradientAt (fun w => v z.1 + (fderiv ℝ v z.1) (w - z.1))
      ((InnerProductSpace.toDual ℝ _).symm (fderiv ℝ v z.1)) y
    rw [hasGradientAt_iff_hasFDerivAt, LinearIsometryEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
    have h_clm_at : HasFDerivAt (fun w : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) =>
        (fderiv ℝ v z.1) (w - z.1)) (fderiv ℝ v z.1) y := by
      have h := (fderiv ℝ v z.1).hasFDerivAt.comp y ((hasFDerivAt_id y).sub_const z.1)
      rw [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_id] at h
      exact h
    exact h_clm_at.const_add (v z.1)
  have h_grad_cont_global : Continuous (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × ↥S =>
      grad_fSub p.1 p.2) :=
    (InnerProductSpace.toDual ℝ _).symm.continuous.comp
      (h_fderiv_cont.comp (continuous_subtype_val.comp continuous_snd))
  have h_grad_cont : ContinuousOn (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × ↥S =>
      grad_fSub p.1 p.2) ((interior s.X) ×ˢ univ) := h_grad_cont_global.continuousOn
  -- Danskin.valueFunction fSub = pStar v S, allowing Danskin's theorem to apply.
  have h_value_eq : ∀ y, Danskin.valueFunction fSub y = pStar v S y := by
    intro y
    change (⨆ z : ↥S, v z.1 + (fderiv ℝ v z.1) (y - z.1))
      = sSup ((fun x => v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (y - x)) '' S)
    rw [← sSup_range]
    congr 1
    ext c
    simp only [Set.mem_range, Set.mem_image]
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · rintro ⟨z, hz⟩; exact ⟨z.1, z.2, hz⟩
    · rintro ⟨x, hxS, hc⟩; exact ⟨⟨x, hxS⟩, hc⟩
  have h_argmax_ne : (Danskin.argmax_iSup fSub ω).Nonempty :=
    Danskin.argmax_iSup_nonempty fSub
      (h_fSub_cont.comp (Continuous.prodMk continuous_const continuous_id))
  have h_grad_const : ∀ z ∈ Danskin.argmax_iSup fSub ω, grad_fSub ω z = g_vec := by
    intro z hz
    have hz_eq : fSub ω z = Danskin.valueFunction fSub ω := hz
    have hx_chi : z.1 ∈ chi_corr v S ω := by
      refine ⟨z.2, ?_⟩
      change v z.1 + (fderiv ℝ v z.1) (ω - z.1) = pStar v S ω
      rw [← h_value_eq ω]; exact hz_eq
    have h_fderiv_eq : fderiv ℝ v z.1 = g_clm := hg z.1 hx_chi
    change (InnerProductSpace.toDual ℝ _).symm (fderiv ℝ v z.1) =
      (InnerProductSpace.toDual ℝ _).symm g_clm
    rw [h_fderiv_eq]
  have h_gradient : HasGradientAt (Danskin.valueFunction fSub) g_vec ω :=
    Danskin.hasGradientAt_iSup_of_const_grad fSub grad_fSub (interior s.X) isOpen_interior
      h_cont h_diff h_grad_cont ω hω g_vec h_argmax_ne h_grad_const
  rw [show pStar v S = Danskin.valueFunction fSub from funext fun y => (h_value_eq y).symm]
  exact h_gradient.differentiableAt

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- **Basic properties of `Γ_x`.**

For `x ∈ S` (assumed to be active in the sense `v x = pStar v S x`), the contact-set fiber `Γ_x` is
compact convex, contains `x`, and equals the argmin of `ω ↦ pStar v S ω - (fderiv ℝ v x) ω` over
`s.X`. -/
lemma Gamma_x_isCompact_isConvex_mem_argMin
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS : S ⊆ s.X)
    {x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (hx : x ∈ S)
    (hx_active : v x = pStar v S x) :
    IsCompact (Gamma_x s v S x) ∧ Convex ℝ (Gamma_x s v S x) ∧
      x ∈ Gamma_x s v S x ∧
      Gamma_x s v S x =
        {ω ∈ s.X | ∀ ω' ∈ s.X,
          pStar v S ω - (fderiv ℝ v x) ω ≤ pStar v S ω' - (fderiv ℝ v x) ω'} := by
  have h_tangent_le : ∀ ω, v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x) ≤ pStar v S ω := fun ω =>
    le_csSup (pStar_image_bddAbove s hv_diff hS ω) ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  -- g(ω) := pStar v S ω - (v x + fderiv v x · (ω - x)) is nonneg; Γ_x = s.X ∩ {g ≤ 0}.
  set g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ :=
    fun ω => pStar v S ω - (v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) with hg_def
  have h_g_nonneg : ∀ ω, 0 ≤ g ω := fun ω => sub_nonneg.mpr (h_tangent_le ω)
  have h_Γ_eq_inter : Gamma_x s v S x = s.X ∩ {ω | g ω ≤ 0} := by
    ext ω
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · rintro ⟨hωX, h_eq⟩
      refine ⟨hωX, ?_⟩
      change g ω ≤ 0
      have : g ω = 0 := by
        change pStar v S ω - (v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) = 0
        linarith [h_eq]
      linarith
    · rintro ⟨hωX, h_le⟩
      refine ⟨hωX, ?_⟩
      have h_g_zero : g ω = 0 := le_antisymm h_le (h_g_nonneg ω)
      change pStar v S ω = v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)
      linarith [h_g_zero]
  obtain ⟨y₀, hy₀_int⟩ := s.X_interior
  have hy₀_X : y₀ ∈ s.X := interior_subset hy₀_int
  have h_fderiv_cont : Continuous (fderiv ℝ v) :=
    hv_diff.continuous_fderiv one_ne_zero
  have h_norm_cont : Continuous (fun y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => ‖fderiv ℝ v y‖) :=
    h_fderiv_cont.norm
  have h_M_compact : IsCompact ((fun y => ‖fderiv ℝ v y‖) '' s.X) :=
    s.X_compact.image h_norm_cont
  have h_M_bdd : BddAbove ((fun y => ‖fderiv ℝ v y‖) '' s.X) := h_M_compact.bddAbove
  set M : ℝ := sSup ((fun y => ‖fderiv ℝ v y‖) '' s.X) with hM_def
  have h_M_y₀ : ‖fderiv ℝ v y₀‖ ∈ ((fun y => ‖fderiv ℝ v y‖) '' s.X) :=
    Set.mem_image_of_mem _ hy₀_X
  have h_M_nn : 0 ≤ M :=
    le_csSup_of_le h_M_bdd h_M_y₀ (norm_nonneg _)
  set L : NNReal := ⟨M, h_M_nn⟩ with hL_def
  have h_slope : ∀ y ∈ S, ‖fderiv ℝ v y‖ ≤ (L : ℝ) := fun y hyS =>
    le_csSup h_M_bdd (Set.mem_image_of_mem _ (hS hyS))
  have h_pStar_lip : LipschitzWith L (pStar v S) := pStar_lipschitzWith s hv_diff hS h_slope
  have h_pStar_cont : Continuous (pStar v S) := h_pStar_lip.continuous
  have h_lin_cont : Continuous (fun ω => v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) :=
    continuous_const.add ((fderiv ℝ v x).continuous.comp (continuous_id.sub continuous_const))
  have h_g_cont : Continuous g := h_pStar_cont.sub h_lin_cont
  have h_pStar_convex : ConvexOn ℝ s.X (pStar v S) := pStar_convexOn s hv_diff hS
  have h_L_concave : ConcaveOn ℝ s.X (fun ω => (fderiv ℝ v x) ω) :=
    (fderiv ℝ v x).toLinearMap.concaveOn s.X_convex
  have h_shift_concave : ConcaveOn ℝ s.X (fun ω => (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) := by
    have h_eq :
        (fun ω : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) =
          (fun ω => (fderiv ℝ v x) ω) + fun _ => -(fderiv ℝ v x) x := by
      ext ω
      change (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x) = (fderiv ℝ v x) ω + (-(fderiv ℝ v x) x)
      rw [map_sub]; ring
    rw [h_eq]
    exact h_L_concave.add_const _
  have h_aff_concave :
      ConcaveOn ℝ s.X (fun ω => v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) := by
    have h_eq :
        (fun ω : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) =
        (fun ω => (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) + fun _ => v x := by
      ext ω
      rw [Pi.add_apply, add_comm]
    rw [h_eq]
    exact h_shift_concave.add_const _
  have h_g_convex : ConvexOn ℝ s.X g := h_pStar_convex.sub h_aff_concave
  have hΓ_closed : IsClosed (Gamma_x s v S x) := by
    rw [h_Γ_eq_inter]
    exact s.X_compact.isClosed.inter (isClosed_le h_g_cont continuous_const)
  have hΓ_subset : Gamma_x s v S x ⊆ s.X := by
    rw [h_Γ_eq_inter]; exact Set.inter_subset_left
  have h_compact : IsCompact (Gamma_x s v S x) :=
    s.X_compact.of_isClosed_subset hΓ_closed hΓ_subset
  have h_convex : Convex ℝ (Gamma_x s v S x) := by
    rw [h_Γ_eq_inter]
    have h_set_eq :
        s.X ∩ {ω | g ω ≤ 0} = {x | x ∈ s.X ∧ g x ≤ 0} := by
      ext ω; rfl
    rw [h_set_eq]
    exact h_g_convex.convex_le 0
  have h_mem : x ∈ Gamma_x s v S x := by
    refine ⟨hS hx, ?_⟩
    change pStar v S x = v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (x - x)
    rw [sub_self, map_zero, add_zero, hx_active]
  have h_argmin :
      Gamma_x s v S x = {ω ∈ s.X | ∀ ω' ∈ s.X,
        pStar v S ω - (fderiv ℝ v x) ω ≤ pStar v S ω' - (fderiv ℝ v x) ω'} := by
    ext ω
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · rintro ⟨hωX, h_eq⟩
      refine ⟨hωX, ?_⟩
      intro ω' hω'X
      have h_omega : pStar v S ω - (fderiv ℝ v x) ω = v x - (fderiv ℝ v x) x := by
        have : (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x) = (fderiv ℝ v x) ω - (fderiv ℝ v x) x :=
          map_sub _ _ _
        linarith [h_eq, this]
      have h_omega' : v x - (fderiv ℝ v x) x ≤ pStar v S ω' - (fderiv ℝ v x) ω' := by
        have h_t := h_tangent_le ω'
        have : (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω' - x) = (fderiv ℝ v x) ω' - (fderiv ℝ v x) x :=
          map_sub _ _ _
        linarith [h_t, this]
      linarith
    · rintro ⟨hωX, h_min⟩
      refine ⟨hωX, ?_⟩
      have h_at_x := h_min x (hS hx)
      have h_pStar_x : pStar v S x = v x := hx_active.symm
      rw [h_pStar_x] at h_at_x
      have h_le : pStar v S ω ≤ v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x) := by
        have h_subst : (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x) = (fderiv ℝ v x) ω - (fderiv ℝ v x) x :=
          map_sub _ _ _
        linarith [h_at_x, h_subst]
      exact le_antisymm h_le (h_tangent_le ω)
  exact ⟨h_compact, h_convex, h_mem, h_argmin⟩

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- Equal gradients imply equal contact fibers.

If `x, y ∈ S` (active) and `∇v(x) = ∇v(y)`, then `Γ_x = Γ_y`. -/
lemma Gamma_x_eq_of_fderiv_eq
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS : S ⊆ s.X)
    {x y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (hx : x ∈ S) (hy : y ∈ S)
    (hx_active : v x = pStar v S x) (hy_active : v y = pStar v S y)
    (h_grad : fderiv ℝ v x = fderiv ℝ v y) :
    Gamma_x s v S x = Gamma_x s v S y := by
  obtain ⟨_, _, _, h_argmin_x⟩ :=
    Gamma_x_isCompact_isConvex_mem_argMin s hv_diff hS hx hx_active
  obtain ⟨_, _, _, h_argmin_y⟩ :=
    Gamma_x_isCompact_isConvex_mem_argMin s hv_diff hS hy hy_active
  rw [h_argmin_x, h_argmin_y, h_grad]

/-- **Relative-interior extension lemma.**

If `C ⊆ V` is convex (in a finite-dimensional real normed space), `x ∈ relint C` and `y ∈ C`, then
there exist `z ∈ C` and `μ ∈ (0, 1)` such that `x = μ • y + (1 - μ) • z`.  Geometrically: A
relative-interior point of a convex set lies strictly inside the segment from any other point of
the set to a third point in the set. -/
lemma exists_extend_of_mem_intrinsicInterior
    {V : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V] [FiniteDimensional ℝ V]
    -- kept for the statement's contract (relint is only meaningful for convex C); unused
    -- in this proof
    {C : Set V} (_hC : Convex ℝ C)
    {x : V} (hx : x ∈ intrinsicInterior ℝ C)
    {y : V} (hy : y ∈ C) :
    ∃ z ∈ C, ∃ μ : ℝ, 0 < μ ∧ μ < 1 ∧ x = μ • y + (1 - μ) • z := by
  by_cases hxy : x = y
  · refine ⟨x, hxy ▸ hy, (1 : ℝ)/2, by norm_num, by norm_num, ?_⟩
    rw [hxy]; module
  obtain ⟨x_lift, hx_lift_int, hx_lift_eq⟩ := mem_intrinsicInterior.mp hx
  have hy_span : y ∈ affineSpan ℝ C := subset_affineSpan ℝ C hy
  let A : AffineSubspace ℝ V := affineSpan ℝ C
  have hxA : x ∈ A := by rw [← hx_lift_eq]; exact x_lift.2
  have hyA : y ∈ A := hy_span
  let y_lift : ↥A := ⟨y, hyA⟩
  haveI : Nonempty ↥A := ⟨x_lift⟩
  have hd_mem : (x - y) ∈ A.direction :=
    AffineSubspace.vsub_mem_direction hxA hyA
  have hC_lift_open_at : (Subtype.val ⁻¹' C : Set ↥A) ∈ nhds x_lift :=
    mem_interior_iff_mem_nhds.mp hx_lift_int
  rw [Metric.mem_nhds_iff] at hC_lift_open_at
  obtain ⟨ε, hε_pos, hε_ball⟩ := hC_lift_open_at
  have h_norm_pos : 0 < ‖x - y‖ := by
    rw [norm_pos_iff]; exact sub_ne_zero.mpr hxy
  set δ : ℝ := ε / (2 * ‖x - y‖) with hδ_def
  have hδ_pos : 0 < δ := by positivity
  let d_dir : A.direction := ⟨x - y, hd_mem⟩
  let z_lift : ↥A := (δ • d_dir) +ᵥ x_lift
  have hz_lift_dist : dist z_lift x_lift < ε := by
    have h_dist_eq : dist z_lift x_lift = ‖δ • (x - y)‖ := by
      change dist ((δ • d_dir) +ᵥ x_lift) x_lift = _
      rw [dist_vadd_left]
      rfl
    rw [h_dist_eq, norm_smul, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_pos hδ_pos]
    have h_simp : δ * ‖x - y‖ = ε / 2 := by
      rw [hδ_def]
      field_simp
    rw [h_simp]
    linarith
  have hz_in_lift : z_lift ∈ (Subtype.val ⁻¹' C : Set ↥A) := hε_ball hz_lift_dist
  have hz_lift_val : (z_lift : V) = x + δ • (x - y) := by
    change ((δ • d_dir) +ᵥ x_lift : ↥A).val = x + δ • (x - y)
    rw [AffineSubspace.coe_vadd]
    change (δ • (x - y)) + (x_lift : V) = x + δ • (x - y)
    rw [hx_lift_eq, add_comm]
  set z : V := (z_lift : V) with hz_def
  have hz_in : z ∈ C := hz_in_lift
  have hz_eq : z = x + δ • (x - y) := hz_lift_val
  refine ⟨z, hz_in, δ / (1 + δ), ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · positivity
  · rw [div_lt_one (by linarith)]; linarith
  · have h1δ_pos : (0 : ℝ) < 1 + δ := by linarith
    have h1δ_ne : (1 + δ : ℝ) ≠ 0 := h1δ_pos.ne'
    have h_eq_scaled : (1 + δ) • x = δ • y + z := by
      rw [hz_eq]
      module
    have h_one_sub_eq : 1 - δ / (1 + δ) = 1 / (1 + δ) := by
      field_simp
      ring
    rw [h_one_sub_eq]
    have h_inv_smul : (1 + δ)⁻¹ • ((1 + δ) • x) = x := by
      rw [smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ h1δ_ne, one_smul]
    have h_step : (1 + δ)⁻¹ • ((1 + δ) • x) = (1 + δ)⁻¹ • (δ • y + z) := by
      rw [h_eq_scaled]
    rw [h_inv_smul] at h_step
    rw [h_step, smul_add, smul_smul]
    rw [show (1 + δ)⁻¹ * δ = δ / (1 + δ) by rw [div_eq_inv_mul, mul_comm]]
    rw [show ((1 + δ)⁻¹ : ℝ) = 1 / (1 + δ) by rw [one_div]]

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- If the relative interior of `Γ_x` meets `Γ_y`, then `Γ_x ⊆ Γ_y`. -/
lemma Gamma_x_subset_of_intrinsicInterior_inter_nonempty
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS : S ⊆ s.X)
    {x y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (hx : x ∈ S) (hy : y ∈ S)
    -- hy_active kept for the statement's contract (y ranges over active points); unused here
    (hx_active : v x = pStar v S x) (_hy_active : v y = pStar v S y)
    (h_inter :
      (intrinsicInterior ℝ (Gamma_x s v S x) ∩ Gamma_x s v S y).Nonempty) :
    Gamma_x s v S x ⊆ Gamma_x s v S y := by
  obtain ⟨ω_star, hω_star_relint, hω_star_in_y⟩ := h_inter
  obtain ⟨_, h_convex_x, _, _⟩ :=
    Gamma_x_isCompact_isConvex_mem_argMin s hv_diff hS hx hx_active
  have h_tangent_le_y : ∀ ω, v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω - y) ≤ pStar v S ω := fun ω =>
    le_csSup (pStar_image_bddAbove s hv_diff hS ω) ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
  have hω_star_in_x : ω_star ∈ Gamma_x s v S x := intrinsicInterior_subset hω_star_relint
  intro ω' hω'_in_x
  obtain ⟨ω'', hω''_in_x, μ, hμ_pos, hμ_lt_one, hω_star_combo⟩ :=
    exists_extend_of_mem_intrinsicInterior h_convex_x hω_star_relint hω'_in_x
  have h_pStar_omega_star : pStar v S ω_star = v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω_star - x) :=
    hω_star_in_x.2
  have h_pStar_omega' : pStar v S ω' = v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω' - x) := hω'_in_x.2
  have h_pStar_omega'' : pStar v S ω'' = v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω'' - x) := hω''_in_x.2
  have h_affine_pStar : pStar v S ω_star = μ * pStar v S ω' + (1 - μ) * pStar v S ω'' := by
    rw [h_pStar_omega_star, h_pStar_omega', h_pStar_omega'']
    have h_combo_sub : ω_star - x = μ • (ω' - x) + (1 - μ) • (ω'' - x) := by
      rw [hω_star_combo]; module
    rw [h_combo_sub]
    rw [(fderiv ℝ v x).map_add, (fderiv ℝ v x).map_smul, (fderiv ℝ v x).map_smul,
        smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
    ring
  have h_pStar_omega_star_y : pStar v S ω_star = v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω_star - y) :=
    hω_star_in_y.2
  have h_tan_omega' : v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω' - y) ≤ pStar v S ω' := h_tangent_le_y ω'
  have h_tan_omega'' : v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω'' - y) ≤ pStar v S ω'' := h_tangent_le_y ω''
  -- The tangent at y of the convex combination ω_star = μω' + (1-μ)ω'' equals the convex
  -- combination of the tangent values, by linearity of fderiv v y.
  have h_tan_combo : v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω_star - y) =
      μ * (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω' - y)) +
        (1 - μ) * (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω'' - y)) := by
    have h_combo_sub_y : ω_star - y = μ • (ω' - y) + (1 - μ) • (ω'' - y) := by
      rw [hω_star_combo]; module
    rw [h_combo_sub_y]
    rw [(fderiv ℝ v y).map_add, (fderiv ℝ v y).map_smul, (fderiv ℝ v y).map_smul,
        smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
    ring
  -- Since pStar(ω*) = μ pStar(ω') + (1-μ) pStar(ω'') and equals the tangent at y, and
  -- each tangent term is ≤ the corresponding pStar value, the differences must vanish.
  have h_one_sub_pos : 0 < 1 - μ := by linarith
  have h_equality_sum :
      μ * pStar v S ω' + (1 - μ) * pStar v S ω'' =
        μ * (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω' - y)) +
          (1 - μ) * (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω'' - y)) := by
    linarith [h_affine_pStar, h_pStar_omega_star_y, h_tan_combo]
  have h_zero_sum :
      μ * (pStar v S ω' - (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω' - y))) +
        (1 - μ) * (pStar v S ω'' - (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω'' - y))) = 0 := by
    linarith [h_equality_sum]
  have h_nn_a : 0 ≤ μ * (pStar v S ω' - (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω' - y))) :=
    mul_nonneg hμ_pos.le (by linarith)
  have h_nn_b :
      0 ≤ (1 - μ) * (pStar v S ω'' - (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω'' - y))) :=
    mul_nonneg h_one_sub_pos.le (by linarith)
  have h_a_zero : μ * (pStar v S ω' - (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω' - y))) = 0 := by
    linarith
  have h_pStar_omega'_y : pStar v S ω' = v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω' - y) := by
    have h_factor : pStar v S ω' - (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω' - y)) = 0 := by
      have hμ_ne : μ ≠ 0 := hμ_pos.ne'
      have h_eq_mul : μ * (pStar v S ω' - (v y + (fderiv ℝ v y) (ω' - y))) = μ * 0 := by
        rw [mul_zero]; exact h_a_zero
      exact mul_left_cancel₀ hμ_ne h_eq_mul
    linarith
  have hω'_in_X : ω' ∈ s.X := hω'_in_x.1
  exact ⟨hω'_in_X, h_pStar_omega'_y⟩

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- If the relative interiors of `Γ_x` and `Γ_y` intersect, then `Γ_x = Γ_y`. The statement uses
`intrinsicInterior` for relative interior. -/
lemma Gamma_x_eq_of_intrinsicInterior_inter_nonempty
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS : S ⊆ s.X)
    {x y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (hx : x ∈ S) (hy : y ∈ S)
    (hx_active : v x = pStar v S x) (hy_active : v y = pStar v S y)
    (h_inter :
      (intrinsicInterior ℝ (Gamma_x s v S x) ∩
        intrinsicInterior ℝ (Gamma_x s v S y)).Nonempty) :
    Gamma_x s v S x = Gamma_x s v S y := by
  obtain ⟨ω_star, hω_star_x_relint, hω_star_y_relint⟩ := h_inter
  have h_xy : (intrinsicInterior ℝ (Gamma_x s v S x) ∩ Gamma_x s v S y).Nonempty :=
    ⟨ω_star, hω_star_x_relint, intrinsicInterior_subset hω_star_y_relint⟩
  have h_yx : (intrinsicInterior ℝ (Gamma_x s v S y) ∩ Gamma_x s v S x).Nonempty :=
    ⟨ω_star, hω_star_y_relint, intrinsicInterior_subset hω_star_x_relint⟩
  have h_x_sub_y : Gamma_x s v S x ⊆ Gamma_x s v S y :=
    Gamma_x_subset_of_intrinsicInterior_inter_nonempty s hv_diff hS hx hy
      hx_active hy_active h_xy
  have h_y_sub_x : Gamma_x s v S y ⊆ Gamma_x s v S x :=
    Gamma_x_subset_of_intrinsicInterior_inter_nonempty s hv_diff hS hy hx
      hy_active hx_active h_yx
  exact Set.Subset.antisymm h_x_sub_y h_y_sub_x

/-! #### Pointwise singleton claim

Under the standing assumptions, the contact correspondence is single-valued at almost every
point of `int s.X`. -/

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- **Pointwise subsingleton criterion.**

At any `ω ∈ interior s.X` where `pStar v S` is differentiable, under
`MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v`, active-set membership `S ⊆ S_star v S`, and the majorization
`v ≤ pStar v S` on `s.X` (which holds for `S = supp(π_X)` of any optimal joint by
`optimality_implies_pStar_majorizes`), the contact correspondence `chi_corr v S ω` is a
subsingleton. -/
lemma MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable.chi_corr_subsingleton_at
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hDiff : MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS : S ⊆ s.X)
    (hS_active : S ⊆ S_star s v S)
    (hpStar_ge_v : ∀ y ∈ s.X, v y ≤ pStar v S y)
    {ω : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (hω : ω ∈ interior s.X)
    (h_diff : DifferentiableAt ℝ (pStar v S) ω)
    {x y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    (hx : x ∈ chi_corr v S ω) (hy : y ∈ chi_corr v S ω) :
    x = y := by
  by_contra hxy
  have h_grad : fderiv ℝ v x = fderiv ℝ v y :=
    fderiv_v_eq_of_chi_corr_at_diff s hDiff.v_C1 hS hω h_diff hx hy
  obtain ⟨hxS, _⟩ := hx
  obtain ⟨hyS, _⟩ := hy
  have hxX : x ∈ s.X := hS hxS
  have hyX : y ∈ s.X := hS hyS
  have hx_active : v x = pStar v S x := (hS_active hxS).2
  have hy_active : v y = pStar v S y := (hS_active hyS).2
  have h_Γ_eq : Gamma_x s v S x = Gamma_x s v S y :=
    Gamma_x_eq_of_fderiv_eq s hDiff.v_C1 hS hxS hyS hx_active hy_active h_grad
  obtain ⟨_, h_convex_x, h_mem_xx, _⟩ :=
    Gamma_x_isCompact_isConvex_mem_argMin s hDiff.v_C1 hS hxS hx_active
  obtain ⟨_, _, h_mem_yy, _⟩ :=
    Gamma_x_isCompact_isConvex_mem_argMin s hDiff.v_C1 hS hyS hy_active
  have h_y_in_Γx : y ∈ Gamma_x s v S x := by rw [h_Γ_eq]; exact h_mem_yy
  have h_pStar_y : pStar v S y = v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (y - x) := h_y_in_Γx.2
  have h_dir : (fderiv ℝ v x) (y - x) = v y - v x := by
    rw [hy_active, h_pStar_y]; ring
  have h_b : v x - (fderiv ℝ v x) x = v y - (fderiv ℝ v y) y := by
    have h_split : (fderiv ℝ v x) (y - x) = (fderiv ℝ v x) y - (fderiv ℝ v x) x :=
      map_sub _ _ _
    have h_y_at_y : (fderiv ℝ v y) y = (fderiv ℝ v x) y := by rw [h_grad]
    rw [h_y_at_y]
    linarith [h_dir, h_split]
  have h_xy_seg : ∀ t : ℝ, t ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1 →
      t • x + (1 - t) • y ∈ Gamma_x s v S x := by
    intro t ht
    exact h_convex_x h_mem_xx h_y_in_Γx ht.1 (by linarith [ht.2]) (by ring)
  have h_c : ∀ t ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1,
      t * v x + (1 - t) * v y ≥ v (t • x + (1 - t) • y) := by
    intro t ht
    have hz_mem : t • x + (1 - t) • y ∈ Gamma_x s v S x := h_xy_seg t ht
    obtain ⟨hz_X, hz_eq⟩ := hz_mem
    have h_z_sub : (t • x + (1 - t) • y) - x = (1 - t) • (y - x) := by
      module
    have h_lin : (fderiv ℝ v x) ((t • x + (1 - t) • y) - x) =
        (1 - t) * (fderiv ℝ v x) (y - x) := by
      rw [h_z_sub, map_smul, smul_eq_mul]
    have h_pStar_z : pStar v S (t • x + (1 - t) • y) = t * v x + (1 - t) * v y := by
      rw [hz_eq, h_lin, h_dir]; ring
    have h_v_le : v (t • x + (1 - t) • y) ≤ pStar v S (t • x + (1 - t) • y) :=
      hpStar_ge_v _ hz_X
    rw [h_pStar_z] at h_v_le
    exact h_v_le
  exact hDiff.v_genericity x hxX y hyX hxy h_grad h_b h_c

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- Under `MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v`, active-set membership `S ⊆ S_star v S`, a gradient
bound on `S`, and the majorization `v ≤ pStar v S` on `s.X`, the contact correspondence
`chi_corr v S ω` is a singleton for prior-pushforward-a.e. `ω ∈ int s.X`. -/
lemma MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable.chi_corr_singleton_ae
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ}
    (hDiff : MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v)
    {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))} (hS : S ⊆ s.X) (hS_ne : S.Nonempty)
    (hS_closed : IsClosed S)
    (hS_active : S ⊆ S_star s v S)
    {L : NNReal} (h_slope : ∀ x ∈ S, ‖fderiv ℝ v x‖ ≤ (L : ℝ))
    (hpStar_ge_v : ∀ y ∈ s.X, v y ≤ pStar v S y) :
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m,
      ω ∈ interior s.X → ∃! x, x ∈ chi_corr v S ω := by
  have h_pStar_lip : LipschitzWith L (pStar v S) :=
    pStar_lipschitzWith s hDiff.v_C1 hS h_slope
  have h_ae_diff : ∀ᵐ ω ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m,
      DifferentiableAt ℝ (pStar v S) ω :=
    ae_differentiableAt_of_lipschitz_absolutelyContinuous
      hDiff.prior_pushforward_AC h_pStar_lip
  filter_upwards [h_ae_diff] with ω h_diff hω
  have h_subsingleton : ∀ x y, x ∈ chi_corr v S ω → y ∈ chi_corr v S ω → x = y :=
    fun x y hx hy => MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable.chi_corr_subsingleton_at
      s hDiff hS hS_active hpStar_ge_v hω h_diff hx hy
  have h_S_compact : IsCompact S := s.X_compact.of_isClosed_subset hS_closed hS
  have h_v_cont : Continuous v := hDiff.v_C1.continuous
  have h_fderiv_cont : Continuous (fderiv ℝ v) :=
    hDiff.v_C1.continuous_fderiv one_ne_zero
  have h_g_cont : Continuous
      (fun x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) :=
    h_v_cont.add (h_fderiv_cont.clm_apply (continuous_const.sub continuous_id))
  obtain ⟨x_star, hx_star_S, h_x_star_max⟩ :=
    h_S_compact.exists_isMaxOn hS_ne h_g_cont.continuousOn
  have h_bdd : BddAbove
      ((fun x => v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) '' S) :=
    pStar_image_bddAbove s hDiff.v_C1 hS ω
  have h_g_image_ne : ((fun x => v x + (fderiv ℝ v x) (ω - x)) '' S).Nonempty :=
    hS_ne.image _
  have h_x_star_eq : v x_star + (fderiv ℝ v x_star) (ω - x_star) = pStar v S ω := by
    refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
    · exact le_csSup h_bdd ⟨x_star, hx_star_S, rfl⟩
    · refine csSup_le h_g_image_ne ?_
      rintro b ⟨y, hyS, rfl⟩
      exact h_x_star_max hyS
  have hx_star_chi : x_star ∈ chi_corr v S ω := ⟨hx_star_S, h_x_star_eq⟩
  refine ⟨x_star, hx_star_chi, ?_⟩
  intro y hy
  exact h_subsingleton y x_star hy hx_star_chi

omit [T2Space Ω] [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω]
  [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- **Chi-selector extraction.**

Given a joint `pi` with active set `S` satisfying `ConditionM` (which packages feasibility and,
equivalently, optimality of `pi`) and `S ⊆ S_star v S`, under `MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v`,
there is a measurable selector `chi : Ω → ℝⁿ` such that `pi`-a.e. the joint's `x`-coordinate equals
`chi` of the state, and `chi` lands in `S` prior-a.e.

The selector is read off the `ConditionM` data plus differentiability alone: The interior-support
mass is recovered internally from `hDiff.prior_pushforward_AC`, so no separate dual-price
regularity or optimality hypotheses are needed. -/
lemma exists_chi_of_optimal_joint
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ} {L : NNReal}
    (hv_lip : LipschitzWith L (fun x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => v x))
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    [s.prior.toMeasure.IsOpenPosMeasure]
    (hDiff : MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v)
    (pi : ProbDist (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω))
    (S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))
    (hM : ConditionM s v pi S)
    (hS_sub : S ⊆ S_star s v S) :
    ∃ chi : Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n),
      Measurable chi ∧
      (∀ᵐ p ∂pi.toMeasure, p.1 = chi p.2) ∧
      (∀ᵐ ω ∂s.prior.toMeasure, chi ω ∈ S) := by
  have hpi : pi ∈ feasibleJoint s := hM.feasible
  have hS_subX : S ⊆ s.X := by
    rw [hM.S_eq_support]
    have h_X_closed : IsClosed (s.X : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) :=
      s.X_compact.isClosed
    have h_pre_closed : IsClosed
        ((Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
          ⁻¹' s.X) :=
      h_X_closed.preimage continuous_fst
    have h_pre_ae : (Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω →
        EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) ⁻¹' s.X ∈ MeasureTheory.ae pi.toMeasure := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.mem_ae_iff]
      exact (MeasureTheory.prob_compl_eq_zero_iff
        (h_X_closed.measurableSet.preimage measurable_fst)).mpr hpi.fst_supportsOn
    have h_supp_sub :
        pi.toMeasure.support ⊆ (Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω →
          EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) ⁻¹' s.X :=
      MeasureTheory.Measure.support_subset_of_isClosed h_pre_closed h_pre_ae
    rintro x ⟨p, hp_supp, rfl⟩
    exact h_supp_sub hp_supp
  have h_supp_compact : IsCompact pi.toMeasure.support := by
    have h_X_compact : IsCompact (s.X : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) := s.X_compact
    have h_Ω_compact : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set Ω) := isCompact_univ
    have h_prod_compact : IsCompact (s.X ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set Ω)) :=
      h_X_compact.prod h_Ω_compact
    apply h_prod_compact.of_isClosed_subset MeasureTheory.Measure.isClosed_support
    intro p hp
    refine ⟨?_, Set.mem_univ _⟩
    have : p.1 ∈ S := by rw [hM.S_eq_support]; exact ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    exact hS_subX this
  have hS_closed : IsClosed S := by
    rw [hM.S_eq_support]
    exact (h_supp_compact.image continuous_fst).isClosed
  have hS_ne : S.Nonempty := hM.activeSet_nonempty
  have h_slope : ∀ x ∈ S, ‖fderiv ℝ v x‖ ≤ (L : ℝ) :=
    fun x _ => norm_fderiv_le_of_lipschitz ℝ hv_lip
  have hpStar_ge_v : ∀ y ∈ s.X, v y ≤ pStar v S y := hM.pStar_majorizes
  have h_singleton_implication :
      ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m,
        ω' ∈ interior s.X → ∃! x, x ∈ chi_corr v S ω' :=
    MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable.chi_corr_singleton_ae s hDiff hS_subX hS_ne hS_closed
      hS_sub h_slope hpStar_ge_v
  have h_prior_map_int : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) = 1 := by
    have h_mX : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) s.X = 1 := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable s.X_compact.isClosed.measurableSet]
      have : s.m ⁻¹' s.X = Set.univ := by
        ext ω; simp [s.m_mem_X]
      rw [this]
      exact MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure.measure_univ
    have h_front_null :
        (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (frontier s.X) = 0 := by
      apply hDiff.prior_pushforward_AC
      exact Convex.addHaar_frontier _ s.X_convex
    have h_sX_eq : s.X = interior s.X ∪ frontier s.X := by
      conv_lhs => rw [← s.X_compact.isClosed.closure_eq]
      exact closure_eq_interior_union_frontier _
    rw [h_sX_eq] at h_mX
    have h_le_one : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) ≤ 1 := by
      have h_total : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) Set.univ = 1 := by
        rw [MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable MeasurableSet.univ]
        simp
      calc (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X)
          ≤ (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) Set.univ :=
            MeasureTheory.measure_mono (Set.subset_univ _)
        _ = 1 := h_total
    have h_ge_one : 1 ≤ (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) := by
      have h_union_le :=
        MeasureTheory.measure_union_le (μ := s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m)
          (interior s.X) (frontier s.X)
      rw [h_front_null, add_zero] at h_union_le
      exact h_mX ▸ h_union_le
    exact le_antisymm h_le_one h_ge_one
  have h_singleton_ae :
      ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, ∃ x, chi_corr v S ω' = {x} := by
    have h_int_ae : ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, ω' ∈ interior s.X := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]
      have h_compl : {ω' | ¬ ω' ∈ interior s.X} = (interior s.X)ᶜ := rfl
      rw [h_compl]
      haveI : MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) :=
        MeasureTheory.Measure.isProbabilityMeasure_map s.m_measurable.aemeasurable
      exact (MeasureTheory.prob_compl_eq_zero_iff
        isOpen_interior.measurableSet).mpr h_prior_map_int
    filter_upwards [h_singleton_implication, h_int_ae] with ω' h_imp hω'_int
    obtain ⟨x, hx_mem, hx_unique⟩ := h_imp hω'_int
    refine ⟨x, ?_⟩
    ext y
    refine ⟨fun hy => hx_unique y hy, fun hy => ?_⟩
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hy
    rw [hy]; exact hx_mem
  have h_S_compact : IsCompact S :=
    s.X_compact.of_isClosed_subset hS_closed hS_subX
  have h_pStar_cont : Continuous (pStar v S) :=
    (pStar_lipschitzWith s hv_diff hS_subX h_slope).continuous
  have h_chi_corr_graph_closed :
      IsClosed
        {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) |
          p.2 ∈ chi_corr v S p.1} :=
    chi_corr_graph_isClosed hv_diff hS_closed h_pStar_cont
  have h_chi_corr_sub : ∀ ω, chi_corr v S ω ⊆ S := fun _ _ hx => hx.1
  obtain ⟨chi_tilde, h_chi_tilde_meas, Y₀, hY₀_meas, hY₀_full, hY₀_eq⟩ :=
    MeasureTheory.exists_measurable_selection_of_singleton_ae
      (F := chi_corr v S) (K := S)
      h_S_compact h_chi_corr_sub h_chi_corr_graph_closed h_singleton_ae
  have hY₀_ae_prior_map : ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, ω' ∈ Y₀ := by
    rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]; exact hY₀_full
  have h_chi_tilde_in : ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m,
      chi_tilde ω' ∈ chi_corr v S ω' := by
    filter_upwards [hY₀_ae_prior_map] with ω' hω'
    rw [hY₀_eq ω' hω']; rfl
  refine ⟨chi_tilde ∘ s.m, h_chi_tilde_meas.comp s.m_measurable, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have h_prior_eq_snd : s.prior.toMeasure = pi.toMeasure.map Prod.snd := by
      have h := hpi.marginal
      have h' := congrArg (fun d : ProbDist Ω => (d : Measure Ω)) h
      simp only [ProbDist.map_toMeasure] at h'
      exact h'.symm
    have hY₀_ae_pi : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi.toMeasure, s.m p.2 ∈ Y₀ := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]
      have h_meas_set : MeasurableSet ((fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω
          => s.m p.2) ⁻¹' Y₀) :=
        (s.m_measurable.comp measurable_snd) hY₀_meas
      have h_eq_set : {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω | ¬ s.m p.2 ∈ Y₀}
          = (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => s.m p.2) ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ := rfl
      rw [h_eq_set]
      have : pi.toMeasure ((fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => s.m p.2)
          ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ) = (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) Y₀ᶜ := by
        rw [show ((fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => s.m p.2) ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ)
            = (Prod.snd ⁻¹' (s.m ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ)) from rfl,
          ← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply measurable_snd
            (s.m_measurable hY₀_meas.compl),
          ← h_prior_eq_snd,
          ← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable hY₀_meas.compl]
      rw [this, hY₀_full]
    have h_p1_in_S : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi.toMeasure, p.1 ∈ S := by
      rw [hM.S_eq_support]
      filter_upwards [MeasureTheory.Measure.support_mem_ae (μ := pi.toMeasure)]
        with p hp
      exact ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    filter_upwards [hM.active_ae, hY₀_ae_pi, h_p1_in_S]
      with p hp_active hp_in_Y₀ hp_in_S
    have hp1_in_chi : p.1 ∈ chi_corr v S (s.m p.2) := ⟨hp_in_S, hp_active.symm⟩
    rw [hY₀_eq (s.m p.2) hp_in_Y₀] at hp1_in_chi
    exact hp1_in_chi
  · have h_meas_mem : MeasurableSet {y | chi_tilde y ∈ S} :=
      h_chi_tilde_meas hS_closed.measurableSet
    have h_chi_tilde_in_S :
        ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, chi_tilde ω' ∈ S := by
      filter_upwards [h_chi_tilde_in, h_singleton_ae] with ω' h_in h_sing
      obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := h_sing
      have hx_mem : x ∈ S := by
        have : x ∈ chi_corr v S ω' := by rw [hx]; exact rfl
        exact this.1
      have h_eq : chi_tilde ω' = x := by
        have : chi_tilde ω' ∈ ({x} : Set _) := by rw [← hx]; exact h_in
        exact this
      rw [h_eq]; exact hx_mem
    exact (MeasureTheory.ae_map_iff s.m_measurable.aemeasurable h_meas_mem).mp
      h_chi_tilde_in_S

omit [CompactSpace Ω] [T2Space Ω] [SecondCountableTopology Ω]
  [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω] [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- **Pushforward identity for joint distributions with a graph property.**

If a joint `pi` has `Ω`-marginal equal to `prior` and pi-a.e. the first coordinate equals `chi` of
the second, then `pi` equals the pushforward of `prior` along the graph map `ω ↦ (chi ω, ω)`. -/
lemma joint_eq_pushforward_of_graph_ae
    {n : ℕ} (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    (pi : ProbDist (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω))
    (h_marginal : pi.toMeasure.map Prod.snd = s.prior.toMeasure)
    {chi : Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} (h_chi_meas : Measurable chi)
    (h_graph : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi.toMeasure, p.1 = chi p.2) :
    pi.toMeasure = s.prior.toMeasure.map (fun ω => (chi ω, ω)) := by
  have h_id : pi.toMeasure.map id = pi.toMeasure := MeasureTheory.Measure.map_id
  have h_eq_ae : (id : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω → _) =ᵐ[pi.toMeasure]
      (fun p => (chi p.2, p.2)) := by
    filter_upwards [h_graph] with p hp
    exact Prod.ext hp rfl
  have h_map_congr : pi.toMeasure.map (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω
      => (chi p.2, p.2)) = pi.toMeasure := by
    rw [← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_congr h_eq_ae, h_id]
  have h_factor : (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => (chi p.2, p.2))
      = (fun ω => (chi ω, ω)) ∘ Prod.snd := rfl
  have h_chi_id_meas : Measurable (fun ω : Ω => (chi ω, ω)) :=
    h_chi_meas.prodMk measurable_id
  rw [← h_map_congr, h_factor,
    ← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_map h_chi_id_meas measurable_snd, h_marginal]

omit [T2Space Ω] [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace Ω]
  [Inhabited Ω] in
/-- **Bayes-plausible selector construction.**

Given an optimal joint `pi` with active set `S` satisfying `ConditionM` and `S ⊆ S_star v S`, under
`MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v` there exists a measurable Bayes-plausible selector `χ : Ω → X`
into `S`. -/
lemma exists_bayesPlausibleSelector_of_optimal_joint
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ} {L : NNReal}
    (hv_lip : LipschitzWith L (fun x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => v x))
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    [s.prior.toMeasure.IsOpenPosMeasure]
    (hDiff : MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v)
    (pi : ProbDist (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω))
    (S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))
    (hM : ConditionM s v pi S)
    (hS_sub : S ⊆ S_star s v S) :
    Nonempty (BayesPlausibleSelector s S) := by
  have hpi : pi ∈ feasibleJoint s := hM.feasible
  have hS_subX : S ⊆ s.X := by
    rw [hM.S_eq_support]
    have h_X_closed : IsClosed (s.X : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) :=
      s.X_compact.isClosed
    have h_pre_closed : IsClosed
        ((Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
          ⁻¹' s.X) :=
      h_X_closed.preimage continuous_fst
    have h_pre_ae : (Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω →
        EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) ⁻¹' s.X ∈ MeasureTheory.ae pi.toMeasure := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.mem_ae_iff]
      exact (MeasureTheory.prob_compl_eq_zero_iff
        (h_X_closed.measurableSet.preimage measurable_fst)).mpr hpi.fst_supportsOn
    have h_supp_sub :
        pi.toMeasure.support ⊆ (Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω →
          EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) ⁻¹' s.X :=
      MeasureTheory.Measure.support_subset_of_isClosed h_pre_closed h_pre_ae
    rintro x ⟨p, hp_supp, rfl⟩
    exact h_supp_sub hp_supp
  have h_supp_compact : IsCompact pi.toMeasure.support := by
    have h_X_compact : IsCompact (s.X : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) := s.X_compact
    have h_Ω_compact : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set Ω) :=
      isCompact_univ
    have h_prod_compact : IsCompact (s.X ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set Ω)) :=
      h_X_compact.prod h_Ω_compact
    apply h_prod_compact.of_isClosed_subset MeasureTheory.Measure.isClosed_support
    intro p hp
    refine ⟨?_, Set.mem_univ _⟩
    have : p.1 ∈ S := by rw [hM.S_eq_support]; exact ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    exact hS_subX this
  have hS_closed : IsClosed S := by
    rw [hM.S_eq_support]
    exact (h_supp_compact.image continuous_fst).isClosed
  have hS_ne : S.Nonempty := hM.activeSet_nonempty
  have h_slope : ∀ x ∈ S, ‖fderiv ℝ v x‖ ≤ (L : ℝ) :=
    fun x _ => norm_fderiv_le_of_lipschitz ℝ hv_lip
  have hpStar_ge_v : ∀ y ∈ s.X, v y ≤ pStar v S y := hM.pStar_majorizes
  have h_singleton_implication :
      ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m,
        ω' ∈ interior s.X → ∃! x, x ∈ chi_corr v S ω' :=
    MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable.chi_corr_singleton_ae s hDiff hS_subX hS_ne hS_closed
      hS_sub h_slope hpStar_ge_v
  have h_prior_map_int : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) = 1 := by
    have h_mX : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) s.X = 1 := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable s.X_compact.isClosed.measurableSet]
      have : s.m ⁻¹' s.X = Set.univ := by
        ext ω; simp [s.m_mem_X]
      rw [this]
      exact MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure.measure_univ
    have h_front_null :
        (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (frontier s.X) = 0 := by
      apply hDiff.prior_pushforward_AC
      exact Convex.addHaar_frontier _ s.X_convex
    have h_sX_eq : s.X = interior s.X ∪ frontier s.X := by
      conv_lhs => rw [← s.X_compact.isClosed.closure_eq]
      exact closure_eq_interior_union_frontier _
    rw [h_sX_eq] at h_mX
    have h_le_one : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) ≤ 1 := by
      have h_total : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) Set.univ = 1 := by
        rw [MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable MeasurableSet.univ]
        simp
      calc (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X)
          ≤ (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) Set.univ :=
            MeasureTheory.measure_mono (Set.subset_univ _)
        _ = 1 := h_total
    have h_ge_one : 1 ≤ (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) := by
      have h_union_le :=
        MeasureTheory.measure_union_le (μ := s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m)
          (interior s.X) (frontier s.X)
      rw [h_front_null, add_zero] at h_union_le
      exact h_mX ▸ h_union_le
    exact le_antisymm h_le_one h_ge_one
  have h_singleton_ae :
      ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, ∃ x, chi_corr v S ω' = {x} := by
    have h_int_ae : ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, ω' ∈ interior s.X := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]
      have h_compl : {ω' | ¬ ω' ∈ interior s.X} = (interior s.X)ᶜ := rfl
      rw [h_compl]
      haveI : MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) :=
        MeasureTheory.Measure.isProbabilityMeasure_map s.m_measurable.aemeasurable
      exact (MeasureTheory.prob_compl_eq_zero_iff
        isOpen_interior.measurableSet).mpr h_prior_map_int
    filter_upwards [h_singleton_implication, h_int_ae] with ω' h_imp hω'_int
    obtain ⟨x, hx_mem, hx_unique⟩ := h_imp hω'_int
    refine ⟨x, ?_⟩
    ext y
    refine ⟨fun hy => hx_unique y hy, fun hy => ?_⟩
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hy
    rw [hy]; exact hx_mem
  have h_S_compact : IsCompact S :=
    s.X_compact.of_isClosed_subset hS_closed hS_subX
  have h_pStar_cont : Continuous (pStar v S) :=
    (pStar_lipschitzWith s hv_diff hS_subX h_slope).continuous
  have h_chi_corr_graph_closed :
      IsClosed
        {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) |
          p.2 ∈ chi_corr v S p.1} :=
    chi_corr_graph_isClosed hv_diff hS_closed h_pStar_cont
  have h_chi_corr_sub : ∀ ω, chi_corr v S ω ⊆ S := fun _ _ hx => hx.1
  obtain ⟨chi_tilde, h_chi_tilde_meas, Y₀, hY₀_meas, hY₀_full, hY₀_eq⟩ :=
    MeasureTheory.exists_measurable_selection_of_singleton_ae
      (F := chi_corr v S) (K := S)
      h_S_compact h_chi_corr_sub h_chi_corr_graph_closed h_singleton_ae
  have hY₀_ae_prior_map : ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, ω' ∈ Y₀ := by
    rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]; exact hY₀_full
  have h_chi_tilde_in : ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m,
      chi_tilde ω' ∈ chi_corr v S ω' := by
    filter_upwards [hY₀_ae_prior_map] with ω' hω'
    rw [hY₀_eq ω' hω']; rfl
  refine ⟨{
    chi := chi_tilde ∘ s.m
    chi_meas := h_chi_tilde_meas.comp s.m_measurable
    chi_in_S_ae := ?_
    bayes_plausibility := ?_
  }⟩
  · have h_meas_mem : MeasurableSet {y | chi_tilde y ∈ S} :=
      h_chi_tilde_meas hS_closed.measurableSet
    have h_chi_tilde_in_S :
        ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, chi_tilde ω' ∈ S := by
      filter_upwards [h_chi_tilde_in, h_singleton_ae] with ω' h_in h_sing
      obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := h_sing
      have hx_mem : x ∈ S := by
        have : x ∈ chi_corr v S ω' := by rw [hx]; exact rfl
        exact this.1
      have h_eq : chi_tilde ω' = x := by
        have : chi_tilde ω' ∈ ({x} : Set _) := by rw [← hx]; exact h_in
        exact this
      rw [h_eq]; exact hx_mem
    exact (MeasureTheory.ae_map_iff s.m_measurable.aemeasurable h_meas_mem).mp
      h_chi_tilde_in_S
  · intro x hx_in_S
    set chi : Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) := chi_tilde ∘ s.m with hchi_def
    set cell : Set Ω := chi ⁻¹' {x} with hcell_def
    set A : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) := {x} with hA_def
    have hchi_meas : Measurable chi := h_chi_tilde_meas.comp s.m_measurable
    have hA_meas : MeasurableSet A := measurableSet_singleton x
    have hcell_meas : MeasurableSet cell := hchi_meas hA_meas
    have h_graph : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi.toMeasure, p.1 = chi p.2 := by
      have h_prior_eq_snd : s.prior.toMeasure = pi.toMeasure.map Prod.snd := by
        have h := hpi.marginal
        have h' := congrArg (fun d : ProbDist Ω => (d : Measure Ω)) h
        simp only [ProbDist.map_toMeasure] at h'
        exact h'.symm
      have hY₀_ae_pi : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi.toMeasure, s.m p.2 ∈ Y₀ := by
        rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]
        have h_meas_set : MeasurableSet ((fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω
            => s.m p.2) ⁻¹' Y₀) :=
          (s.m_measurable.comp measurable_snd) hY₀_meas
        have h_eq_set : {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω | ¬ s.m p.2 ∈ Y₀}
            = (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => s.m p.2) ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ := rfl
        rw [h_eq_set]
        have : pi.toMeasure ((fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => s.m p.2)
            ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ) = (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) Y₀ᶜ := by
          rw [show ((fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => s.m p.2) ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ)
              = (Prod.snd ⁻¹' (s.m ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ)) from rfl,
            ← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply measurable_snd
              (s.m_measurable hY₀_meas.compl),
            ← h_prior_eq_snd,
            ← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable hY₀_meas.compl]
        rw [this, hY₀_full]
      have h_p1_in_S : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi.toMeasure, p.1 ∈ S := by
        rw [hM.S_eq_support]
        filter_upwards [MeasureTheory.Measure.support_mem_ae (μ := pi.toMeasure)]
          with p hp
        exact ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
      filter_upwards [hM.active_ae, hY₀_ae_pi, h_p1_in_S]
        with p hp_active hp_in_Y₀ hp_in_S
      have hp1_in_chi : p.1 ∈ chi_corr v S (s.m p.2) := ⟨hp_in_S, hp_active.symm⟩
      rw [hY₀_eq (s.m p.2) hp_in_Y₀] at hp1_in_chi
      exact hp1_in_chi
    refine PiLp.ext (fun i => ?_)
    have h_proj_cont : Continuous (fun y : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => y.ofLp i) :=
      (continuous_apply i).comp (PiLp.continuous_ofLp 2 (fun _ : Fin n => ℝ))
    obtain ⟨R, hR⟩ := s.X_compact.isBounded.exists_norm_le
    have h_X_meas : MeasurableSet (s.X : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) :=
      s.X_compact.isClosed.measurableSet
    have h_fst_meas : MeasurableSet
        ((Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
          ⁻¹' s.X) :=
      h_X_meas.preimage measurable_fst
    have h_ae_p1 : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi.toMeasure, p.1 ∈ s.X := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]
      have h_set_eq :
          {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω | ¬ p.1 ∈ s.X}
            = ((Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
                ⁻¹' s.X)ᶜ := rfl
      rw [h_set_eq, MeasureTheory.prob_compl_eq_zero_iff h_fst_meas]
      exact hpi.fst_supportsOn
    have h_m_meas_pi : Measurable
        (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => (s.m p.2).ofLp i) :=
      (h_proj_cont.measurable.comp s.m_continuous.measurable).comp measurable_snd
    have h_p1_meas_pi : Measurable
        (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => p.1.ofLp i) :=
      h_proj_cont.measurable.comp measurable_fst
    have h_m_int_pi : Integrable
        (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => (s.m p.2).ofLp i) pi.toMeasure := by
      refine Integrable.of_bound h_m_meas_pi.aestronglyMeasurable R ?_
      refine Filter.Eventually.of_forall (fun p => ?_)
      have h_m_i : ‖(s.m p.2).ofLp i‖ ≤ R :=
        (PiLp.norm_apply_le (s.m p.2) i).trans (hR _ (s.m_mem_X p.2))
      simpa using h_m_i
    have h_p1_int_pi : Integrable
        (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => p.1.ofLp i) pi.toMeasure := by
      refine Integrable.of_bound h_p1_meas_pi.aestronglyMeasurable R ?_
      filter_upwards [h_ae_p1] with p hp
      have h_p_i : ‖p.1.ofLp i‖ ≤ R :=
        (PiLp.norm_apply_le p.1 i).trans (hR _ hp)
      simpa using h_p_i
    have h_prior_eq_snd : s.prior.toMeasure = pi.toMeasure.map Prod.snd := by
      have h := hpi.marginal
      have h' := congrArg (fun d : ProbDist Ω => (d : Measure Ω)) h
      simp only [ProbDist.map_toMeasure] at h'
      exact h'.symm
    have h_LHS_to_pi :
        ∫ ω in cell, (s.m ω).ofLp i ∂s.prior.toMeasure
          = ∫ p in (Set.univ : Set _) ×ˢ cell, (s.m p.2).ofLp i ∂pi.toMeasure := by
      rw [h_prior_eq_snd,
        MeasureTheory.setIntegral_map (f := fun ω : Ω => (s.m ω).ofLp i) hcell_meas
          (h_proj_cont.measurable.comp s.m_continuous.measurable).aestronglyMeasurable
          measurable_snd.aemeasurable,
        ← Set.univ_prod (α := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))]
    have h_indicator_swap :
        ∀ᵐ p ∂pi.toMeasure,
          (Set.univ ×ˢ cell).indicator
              (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => (s.m p.2).ofLp i) p
            = (A ×ˢ Set.univ).indicator
              (fun p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω => (s.m p.2).ofLp i) p := by
      filter_upwards [h_graph] with p hp
      by_cases hpx : p.1 = x
      · have hpx_in_A : p.1 ∈ A := by
          rw [hA_def, Set.mem_singleton_iff]; exact hpx
        have h_chi_eq_x : chi p.2 = x := by rw [← hp]; exact hpx
        have hp_in_cell : p.2 ∈ cell := by
          rw [hcell_def, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff]; exact h_chi_eq_x
        have h1 : p ∈ Set.univ ×ˢ cell := ⟨Set.mem_univ _, hp_in_cell⟩
        have h2 : p ∈ A ×ˢ Set.univ := ⟨hpx_in_A, Set.mem_univ _⟩
        rw [Set.indicator_of_mem h1, Set.indicator_of_mem h2]
      · have hpx_notin_A : p.1 ∉ A := by
          rw [hA_def, Set.mem_singleton_iff]; exact hpx
        have h_chi_ne_x : chi p.2 ≠ x := by rw [← hp]; exact hpx
        have hp_notin_cell : p.2 ∉ cell := by
          rw [hcell_def, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff]; exact h_chi_ne_x
        have h1 : p ∉ Set.univ ×ˢ cell := fun hp => hp_notin_cell hp.2
        have h2 : p ∉ A ×ˢ Set.univ := fun hp => hpx_notin_A hp.1
        rw [Set.indicator_of_notMem h1, Set.indicator_of_notMem h2]
    have h_swap_region :
        ∫ p in (Set.univ : Set _) ×ˢ cell, (s.m p.2).ofLp i ∂pi.toMeasure
          = ∫ p in A ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set _), (s.m p.2).ofLp i ∂pi.toMeasure := by
      have h_univ_cell_meas : MeasurableSet
          ((Set.univ : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) ×ˢ cell) :=
        MeasurableSet.univ.prod hcell_meas
      have h_A_univ_meas : MeasurableSet (A ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set Ω)) :=
        hA_meas.prod MeasurableSet.univ
      rw [← MeasureTheory.integral_indicator h_univ_cell_meas,
          ← MeasureTheory.integral_indicator h_A_univ_meas]
      exact MeasureTheory.integral_congr_ae h_indicator_swap
    have h_mart_set := hpi.setIntegral_m_eq_setIntegral_fst_ofLp hA_meas i
    have h_RHS_const :
        ∫ p in A ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set _), p.1.ofLp i ∂pi.toMeasure
          = (pi.toMeasure (A ×ˢ Set.univ)).toReal * x.ofLp i := by
      have h_A_univ_meas : MeasurableSet (A ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set Ω)) :=
        hA_meas.prod MeasurableSet.univ
      have h_eq : ∫ p in A ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set _), p.1.ofLp i ∂pi.toMeasure
          = ∫ p in A ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set _), x.ofLp i ∂pi.toMeasure := by
        refine MeasureTheory.setIntegral_congr_ae h_A_univ_meas
          (Filter.Eventually.of_forall (fun p hp => ?_))
        have hpA : p.1 ∈ A := hp.1
        rw [hA_def, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hpA
        rw [hpA]
      rw [h_eq, MeasureTheory.setIntegral_const, smul_eq_mul,
          MeasureTheory.measureReal_def]
    have h_pi_mass_eq :
        pi.toMeasure (Set.univ ×ˢ cell) = pi.toMeasure (A ×ˢ Set.univ) := by
      apply MeasureTheory.measure_congr
      rw [Filter.eventuallyEq_set]
      filter_upwards [h_graph] with p hp
      by_cases hpx : p.1 = x
      · have hpx_in_A : p.1 ∈ A := by
          rw [hA_def, Set.mem_singleton_iff]; exact hpx
        have h_chi_eq_x : chi p.2 = x := by rw [← hp]; exact hpx
        have hp_in_cell : p.2 ∈ cell := by
          rw [hcell_def, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff]; exact h_chi_eq_x
        exact ⟨fun _ => ⟨hpx_in_A, Set.mem_univ _⟩,
               fun _ => ⟨Set.mem_univ _, hp_in_cell⟩⟩
      · have hpx_notin_A : p.1 ∉ A := by
          rw [hA_def, Set.mem_singleton_iff]; exact hpx
        have h_chi_ne_x : chi p.2 ≠ x := by rw [← hp]; exact hpx
        have hp_notin_cell : p.2 ∉ cell := by
          rw [hcell_def, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff]; exact h_chi_ne_x
        exact ⟨fun h => absurd h.2 hp_notin_cell,
               fun h => absurd h.1 hpx_notin_A⟩
    have h_pi_univ_cell_eq_prior :
        pi.toMeasure (Set.univ ×ˢ cell) = s.prior.toMeasure cell := by
      rw [h_prior_eq_snd, MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply measurable_snd hcell_meas,
          Set.univ_prod]
    have h_mass_real :
        (s.prior.toMeasure cell).toReal = (pi.toMeasure (A ×ˢ Set.univ)).toReal := by
      rw [← h_pi_univ_cell_eq_prior, h_pi_mass_eq]
    have h_LHS_eq : (∫ ω in cell, s.m ω ∂s.prior.toMeasure).ofLp i
        = ∫ ω in cell, (s.m ω).ofLp i ∂s.prior.toMeasure := by
      have h_int_cell : MeasureTheory.Integrable s.m
          ((s.prior.toMeasure).restrict cell) := (s.m_integrable s.prior).restrict
      have := (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) i).integral_comp_comm h_int_cell
      simp only [EuclideanSpace.coe_proj] at this
      exact this.symm
    have h_RHS_eq : ((s.prior.toMeasure cell).toReal • x).ofLp i
        = (s.prior.toMeasure cell).toReal * x.ofLp i := by
      simp [PiLp.smul_apply]
    rw [h_LHS_eq, h_RHS_eq, h_LHS_to_pi, h_swap_region, h_mart_set, h_RHS_const,
        ← h_mass_real]

/-- **Uniqueness of the optimal joint.**

Under `MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v`, two optimal feasible joints coincide. -/
lemma MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable.unique_optimal_joint
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n) (hm_lip : s.IsCoordLipschitz)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ} {L : NNReal}
    (hv_lip : LipschitzWith L (fun x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => v x))
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    (hv_meas : Measurable v) (hv_bdd : ∃ M, ∀ x, |v x| ≤ M)
    (hv_usc : UpperSemicontinuous v)
    (hV_meas : Measurable (s.composedValue v))
    (hV_usc : UpperSemicontinuous (s.composedValue v))
    (h_pcheck_lip : ∀ {p : Ω → ℝ} {K : NNReal},
      LipschitzWith K p → LipschitzOnWith K (convexRoof s p) s.X)
    [s.prior.toMeasure.IsOpenPosMeasure]
    (h_dense : s.X ⊆ closure (Set.range s.m))
    (hDiff : MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v)
    (pi₁ pi₂ : ProbDist (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω))
    (hpi₁ : pi₁ ∈ feasibleJoint s) (hpi₂ : pi₂ ∈ feasibleJoint s)
    (hpi₁_val : ∫ p, v p.1 ∂pi₁.toMeasure = momentPrimal s v)
    (hpi₂_val : ∫ p, v p.1 ∂pi₂.toMeasure = momentPrimal s v) :
    pi₁ = pi₂ := by
  obtain ⟨S₁, hM₁, hS₁_sub⟩ :=
    (optimality_iff_M_with_Sstar s hm_lip hv_lip hv_diff hv_meas hv_bdd hv_usc
      hV_meas hV_usc h_pcheck_lip pi₁ hpi₁ h_dense).mp hpi₁_val
  obtain ⟨S₂, hM₂, hS₂_sub⟩ :=
    (optimality_iff_M_with_Sstar s hm_lip hv_lip hv_diff hv_meas hv_bdd hv_usc
      hV_meas hV_usc h_pcheck_lip pi₂ hpi₂ h_dense).mp hpi₂_val
  obtain ⟨chi₁, h_chi₁_meas, h_graph₁, _h_chi₁_in_S⟩ :=
    exists_chi_of_optimal_joint s hv_lip hv_diff hDiff pi₁ S₁ hM₁ hS₁_sub
  obtain ⟨chi₂, h_chi₂_meas, h_graph₂, _h_chi₂_in_S⟩ :=
    exists_chi_of_optimal_joint s hv_lip hv_diff hDiff pi₂ S₂ hM₂ hS₂_sub
  have h_marg₁ : pi₁.toMeasure.map Prod.snd = s.prior.toMeasure := by
    have h := hpi₁.marginal
    have h' := congrArg (fun d : ProbDist Ω => (d : Measure Ω)) h
    simpa [ProbDist.map_toMeasure] using h'
  have h_marg₂ : pi₂.toMeasure.map Prod.snd = s.prior.toMeasure := by
    have h := hpi₂.marginal
    have h' := congrArg (fun d : ProbDist Ω => (d : Measure Ω)) h
    simpa [ProbDist.map_toMeasure] using h'
  have h_pi₁_eq : pi₁.toMeasure
      = s.prior.toMeasure.map (fun ω => (chi₁ ω, ω)) :=
    joint_eq_pushforward_of_graph_ae s pi₁ h_marg₁ h_chi₁_meas h_graph₁
  have h_pi₂_eq : pi₂.toMeasure
      = s.prior.toMeasure.map (fun ω => (chi₂ ω, ω)) :=
    joint_eq_pushforward_of_graph_ae s pi₂ h_marg₂ h_chi₂_meas h_graph₂
  have h_chi_eq : ∀ᵐ ω ∂s.prior.toMeasure, chi₁ ω = chi₂ ω := by
    obtain ⟨pbar, q, h_struct, h_dual, h_value, h_slack⟩ :=
      prices_for_moments_with_slackness s hm_lip hv_lip hv_meas hv_bdd hv_usc
        hV_meas hV_usc h_pcheck_lip
    have h_slack_pi₁ := h_slack pi₁ hpi₁ hpi₁_val
    have h_slack_pi₂ := h_slack pi₂ hpi₂ hpi₂_val
    have hS₁_active_pbar : ∀ x ∈ S₁, pbar x = v x := by
      rw [hM₁.S_eq_support]
      exact pbar_eq_v_on_active_support s hv_lip hv_meas hv_bdd hpi₁
        h_struct h_slack_pi₁
    have hS₂_active_pbar : ∀ x ∈ S₂, pbar x = v x := by
      rw [hM₂.S_eq_support]
      exact pbar_eq_v_on_active_support s hv_lip hv_meas hv_bdd hpi₂
        h_struct h_slack_pi₂
    have h_pbar_eq_pStar₁ : ∀ y ∈ s.X, pbar y = pStar v S₁ y := by
      have h := pbar_eq_pStar_on_active_support s hm_lip hv_lip hv_diff hv_meas
        hv_bdd hpi₁ hpi₁_val h_struct h_dual h_value h_slack_pi₁ h_dense
      rw [hM₁.S_eq_support]; exact h
    have h_pbar_eq_pStar₂ : ∀ y ∈ s.X, pbar y = pStar v S₂ y := by
      have h := pbar_eq_pStar_on_active_support s hm_lip hv_lip hv_diff hv_meas
        hv_bdd hpi₂ hpi₂_val h_struct h_dual h_value h_slack_pi₂ h_dense
      rw [hM₂.S_eq_support]; exact h
    have h_X_closed : IsClosed (s.X : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) :=
      s.X_compact.isClosed
    have h_pre_X_closed : IsClosed
        ((Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
          ⁻¹' s.X) :=
      h_X_closed.preimage continuous_fst
    have hS₁_subX : S₁ ⊆ s.X := by
      rw [hM₁.S_eq_support]
      have h_pre_ae : (Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω →
          EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) ⁻¹' s.X ∈ MeasureTheory.ae pi₁.toMeasure := by
        rw [MeasureTheory.mem_ae_iff]
        exact (MeasureTheory.prob_compl_eq_zero_iff
          h_pre_X_closed.measurableSet).mpr hpi₁.fst_supportsOn
      have h_supp_sub :
          pi₁.toMeasure.support ⊆ (Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω →
            EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) ⁻¹' s.X :=
        MeasureTheory.Measure.support_subset_of_isClosed h_pre_X_closed h_pre_ae
      rintro x ⟨p, hp_supp, rfl⟩
      exact h_supp_sub hp_supp
    have hS₂_subX : S₂ ⊆ s.X := by
      rw [hM₂.S_eq_support]
      have h_pre_ae : (Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω →
          EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) ⁻¹' s.X ∈ MeasureTheory.ae pi₂.toMeasure := by
        rw [MeasureTheory.mem_ae_iff]
        exact (MeasureTheory.prob_compl_eq_zero_iff
          h_pre_X_closed.measurableSet).mpr hpi₂.fst_supportsOn
      have h_supp_sub :
          pi₂.toMeasure.support ⊆ (Prod.fst : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω →
            EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) ⁻¹' s.X :=
        MeasureTheory.Measure.support_subset_of_isClosed h_pre_X_closed h_pre_ae
      rintro x ⟨p, hp_supp, rfl⟩
      exact h_supp_sub hp_supp
    have h_supp₁_compact : IsCompact pi₁.toMeasure.support := by
      have h_prod_compact : IsCompact (s.X ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set Ω)) :=
        s.X_compact.prod isCompact_univ
      apply h_prod_compact.of_isClosed_subset MeasureTheory.Measure.isClosed_support
      intro p hp
      refine ⟨?_, Set.mem_univ _⟩
      have : p.1 ∈ S₁ := by rw [hM₁.S_eq_support]; exact ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
      exact hS₁_subX this
    have h_supp₂_compact : IsCompact pi₂.toMeasure.support := by
      have h_prod_compact : IsCompact (s.X ×ˢ (Set.univ : Set Ω)) :=
        s.X_compact.prod isCompact_univ
      apply h_prod_compact.of_isClosed_subset MeasureTheory.Measure.isClosed_support
      intro p hp
      refine ⟨?_, Set.mem_univ _⟩
      have : p.1 ∈ S₂ := by rw [hM₂.S_eq_support]; exact ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
      exact hS₂_subX this
    have hS₁_closed : IsClosed S₁ := by
      rw [hM₁.S_eq_support]
      exact (h_supp₁_compact.image continuous_fst).isClosed
    have hS₂_closed : IsClosed S₂ := by
      rw [hM₂.S_eq_support]
      exact (h_supp₂_compact.image continuous_fst).isClosed
    have hS₁_ne : S₁.Nonempty := hM₁.activeSet_nonempty
    set S_union : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) := S₁ ∪ S₂ with hS_union_def
    have hS_union_subX : S_union ⊆ s.X := Set.union_subset hS₁_subX hS₂_subX
    have hS_union_closed : IsClosed S_union := hS₁_closed.union hS₂_closed
    have hS_union_ne : S_union.Nonempty := hS₁_ne.mono Set.subset_union_left
    have hS_union_active_pbar : ∀ x ∈ S_union, pbar x = v x := by
      rintro x (hx | hx)
      · exact hS₁_active_pbar x hx
      · exact hS₂_active_pbar x hx
    have h_pStar_union_le_pbar : ∀ y ∈ s.X, pStar v S_union y ≤ pbar y := by
      intro y hy
      unfold pStar
      refine csSup_le (hS_union_ne.image _) ?_
      rintro _ ⟨x, hxU, rfl⟩
      exact HasMomentPrices.fderiv_isSubgradient_of_active s hv_diff h_struct x
        (hS_union_subX hxU) (hS_union_active_pbar x hxU).symm y hy
    have h_pbar_le_pStar_union : ∀ y ∈ s.X, pbar y ≤ pStar v S_union y := by
      intro y hy
      have h_S₁_sub_union : S₁ ⊆ S_union := Set.subset_union_left
      calc pbar y
          = pStar v S₁ y := h_pbar_eq_pStar₁ y hy
        _ ≤ pStar v S_union y := by
            unfold pStar
            refine csSup_le_csSup
              (pStar_image_bddAbove s hv_diff hS_union_subX y) ?_
              (Set.image_mono h_S₁_sub_union)
            exact hS₁_ne.image _
    have h_pStar_union_eq_pbar : ∀ y ∈ s.X, pStar v S_union y = pbar y :=
      fun y hy => le_antisymm (h_pStar_union_le_pbar y hy) (h_pbar_le_pStar_union y hy)
    have hS_union_active_set : S_union ⊆ S_star s v S_union := by
      intro x hxU
      refine ⟨hxU, ?_⟩
      have hxX : x ∈ s.X := hS_union_subX hxU
      rw [(hS_union_active_pbar x hxU).symm, ← h_pStar_union_eq_pbar x hxX]
    have h_pStar_union_ge_v : ∀ y ∈ s.X, v y ≤ pStar v S_union y :=
      fun y hy => (h_struct.pbar_ge_v y hy).trans (h_pbar_le_pStar_union y hy)
    have h_slope_union : ∀ x ∈ S_union, ‖fderiv ℝ v x‖ ≤ (L : ℝ) :=
      fun _ _ => norm_fderiv_le_of_lipschitz ℝ hv_lip
    have h_singleton_implication :
        ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m,
          ω' ∈ interior s.X → ∃! x, x ∈ chi_corr v S_union ω' :=
      MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable.chi_corr_singleton_ae s hDiff hS_union_subX hS_union_ne
        hS_union_closed hS_union_active_set h_slope_union h_pStar_union_ge_v
    have h_prior_map_int : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) = 1 := by
      have h_mX : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) s.X = 1 := by
        rw [MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable
          s.X_compact.isClosed.measurableSet]
        have : s.m ⁻¹' s.X = Set.univ := by ext ω; simp [s.m_mem_X]
        rw [this]; exact MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure.measure_univ
      have h_front_null : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (frontier s.X) = 0 := by
        apply hDiff.prior_pushforward_AC
        exact Convex.addHaar_frontier _ s.X_convex
      have h_sX_eq : s.X = interior s.X ∪ frontier s.X := by
        conv_lhs => rw [← s.X_compact.isClosed.closure_eq]
        exact closure_eq_interior_union_frontier _
      rw [h_sX_eq] at h_mX
      have h_le_one : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) ≤ 1 := by
        have h_total : (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) Set.univ = 1 := by
          rw [MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable MeasurableSet.univ]; simp
        calc (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X)
            ≤ (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) Set.univ :=
              MeasureTheory.measure_mono (Set.subset_univ _)
          _ = 1 := h_total
      have h_ge_one : 1 ≤ (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) := by
        have h_union_le := MeasureTheory.measure_union_le
          (μ := s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) (interior s.X) (frontier s.X)
        rw [h_front_null, add_zero] at h_union_le
        exact h_mX ▸ h_union_le
      exact le_antisymm h_le_one h_ge_one
    have h_singleton_ae :
        ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, ∃ x, chi_corr v S_union ω' = {x} := by
      have h_int_ae : ∀ᵐ ω' ∂s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m, ω' ∈ interior s.X := by
        rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]
        haveI : MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure (s.prior.toMeasure.map s.m) :=
          MeasureTheory.Measure.isProbabilityMeasure_map s.m_measurable.aemeasurable
        exact (MeasureTheory.prob_compl_eq_zero_iff
          isOpen_interior.measurableSet).mpr h_prior_map_int
      filter_upwards [h_singleton_implication, h_int_ae] with ω' h_imp hω'_int
      obtain ⟨x, hx_mem, hx_unique⟩ := h_imp hω'_int
      refine ⟨x, ?_⟩
      ext y
      refine ⟨fun hy => hx_unique y hy, fun hy => ?_⟩
      rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hy
      rw [hy]; exact hx_mem
    have h_S_union_compact : IsCompact S_union :=
      s.X_compact.of_isClosed_subset hS_union_closed hS_union_subX
    have h_pStar_union_cont : Continuous (pStar v S_union) :=
      (pStar_lipschitzWith s hv_diff hS_union_subX h_slope_union).continuous
    have h_chi_corr_union_graph_closed :
        IsClosed
          {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) |
            p.2 ∈ chi_corr v S_union p.1} :=
      chi_corr_graph_isClosed hv_diff hS_union_closed h_pStar_union_cont
    have h_chi_corr_union_sub : ∀ ω, chi_corr v S_union ω ⊆ S_union :=
      fun _ _ hx => hx.1
    obtain ⟨chi_tilde, h_chi_tilde_meas, Y₀, hY₀_meas, hY₀_full, hY₀_eq⟩ :=
      MeasureTheory.exists_measurable_selection_of_singleton_ae
        (F := chi_corr v S_union) (K := S_union)
        h_S_union_compact h_chi_corr_union_sub h_chi_corr_union_graph_closed
        h_singleton_ae
    have h_marg₁_snd : pi₁.toMeasure.map Prod.snd = s.prior.toMeasure := by
      have h := hpi₁.marginal
      have h' := congrArg (fun d : ProbDist Ω => (d : Measure Ω)) h
      simpa [ProbDist.map_toMeasure] using h'
    have h_marg₂_snd : pi₂.toMeasure.map Prod.snd = s.prior.toMeasure := by
      have h := hpi₂.marginal
      have h' := congrArg (fun d : ProbDist Ω => (d : Measure Ω)) h
      simpa [ProbDist.map_toMeasure] using h'
    have hY₀_ae_pi₁ : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi₁.toMeasure, s.m p.2 ∈ Y₀ := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]
      have h_eq_set : {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω | ¬ s.m p.2 ∈ Y₀}
          = (Prod.snd ⁻¹' (s.m ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ)) := rfl
      rw [h_eq_set,
        ← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply measurable_snd
          (s.m_measurable hY₀_meas.compl),
        h_marg₁_snd,
        ← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable hY₀_meas.compl]
      exact hY₀_full
    have hY₀_ae_pi₂ : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi₂.toMeasure, s.m p.2 ∈ Y₀ := by
      rw [MeasureTheory.ae_iff]
      have h_eq_set : {p : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) × Ω | ¬ s.m p.2 ∈ Y₀}
          = (Prod.snd ⁻¹' (s.m ⁻¹' Y₀ᶜ)) := rfl
      rw [h_eq_set,
        ← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply measurable_snd
          (s.m_measurable hY₀_meas.compl),
        h_marg₂_snd,
        ← MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply s.m_measurable hY₀_meas.compl]
      exact hY₀_full
    have hp1_in_S₁_ae : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi₁.toMeasure, p.1 ∈ S₁ := by
      rw [hM₁.S_eq_support]
      filter_upwards [MeasureTheory.Measure.support_mem_ae (μ := pi₁.toMeasure)]
        with p hp using ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    have hp1_in_S₂_ae : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi₂.toMeasure, p.1 ∈ S₂ := by
      rw [hM₂.S_eq_support]
      filter_upwards [MeasureTheory.Measure.support_mem_ae (μ := pi₂.toMeasure)]
        with p hp using ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    have h_p1_in_corr_pi₁ :
        ∀ᵐ p ∂pi₁.toMeasure, p.1 ∈ chi_corr v S_union (s.m p.2) := by
      filter_upwards [hM₁.active_ae, hp1_in_S₁_ae] with p hp_active hp_in_S₁
      have hmX : s.m p.2 ∈ s.X := s.m_mem_X _
      refine ⟨Or.inl hp_in_S₁, ?_⟩
      have h1 : v p.1 + (fderiv ℝ v p.1) (s.m p.2 - p.1) = pStar v S₁ (s.m p.2) :=
        hp_active.symm
      have h2 : pStar v S₁ (s.m p.2) = pbar (s.m p.2) := (h_pbar_eq_pStar₁ _ hmX).symm
      have h3 : pbar (s.m p.2) = pStar v S_union (s.m p.2) :=
        (h_pStar_union_eq_pbar _ hmX).symm
      rw [h1, h2, h3]
    have h_p1_in_corr_pi₂ :
        ∀ᵐ p ∂pi₂.toMeasure, p.1 ∈ chi_corr v S_union (s.m p.2) := by
      filter_upwards [hM₂.active_ae, hp1_in_S₂_ae] with p hp_active hp_in_S₂
      have hmX : s.m p.2 ∈ s.X := s.m_mem_X _
      refine ⟨Or.inr hp_in_S₂, ?_⟩
      have h1 : v p.1 + (fderiv ℝ v p.1) (s.m p.2 - p.1) = pStar v S₂ (s.m p.2) :=
        hp_active.symm
      have h2 : pStar v S₂ (s.m p.2) = pbar (s.m p.2) := (h_pbar_eq_pStar₂ _ hmX).symm
      have h3 : pbar (s.m p.2) = pStar v S_union (s.m p.2) :=
        (h_pStar_union_eq_pbar _ hmX).symm
      rw [h1, h2, h3]
    have h_chi₁_eq_pi : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi₁.toMeasure,
        chi₁ p.2 = chi_tilde (s.m p.2) := by
      filter_upwards [h_p1_in_corr_pi₁, hY₀_ae_pi₁, h_graph₁]
        with p hp_in_corr hp_in_Y₀ hp_graph
      have h_corr_eq : chi_corr v S_union (s.m p.2) = {chi_tilde (s.m p.2)} :=
        hY₀_eq (s.m p.2) hp_in_Y₀
      rw [h_corr_eq, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hp_in_corr
      rw [← hp_graph]; exact hp_in_corr
    have h_chi₂_eq_pi : ∀ᵐ p ∂pi₂.toMeasure,
        chi₂ p.2 = chi_tilde (s.m p.2) := by
      filter_upwards [h_p1_in_corr_pi₂, hY₀_ae_pi₂, h_graph₂]
        with p hp_in_corr hp_in_Y₀ hp_graph
      have h_corr_eq : chi_corr v S_union (s.m p.2) = {chi_tilde (s.m p.2)} :=
        hY₀_eq (s.m p.2) hp_in_Y₀
      rw [h_corr_eq, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hp_in_corr
      rw [← hp_graph]; exact hp_in_corr
    have h_meas_pred₁ :
        MeasurableSet {ω : Ω | chi₁ ω = chi_tilde (s.m ω)} := by
      have h_diff : Measurable
          (fun ω : Ω => chi₁ ω - chi_tilde (s.m ω)) :=
        h_chi₁_meas.sub (h_chi_tilde_meas.comp s.m_measurable)
      have h_set_eq : {ω : Ω | chi₁ ω = chi_tilde (s.m ω)}
          = (fun ω : Ω => chi₁ ω - chi_tilde (s.m ω)) ⁻¹' ({0} : Set _) := by
        ext ω; simp [sub_eq_zero]
      rw [h_set_eq]
      exact h_diff (measurableSet_singleton 0)
    have h_meas_pred₂ :
        MeasurableSet {ω : Ω | chi₂ ω = chi_tilde (s.m ω)} := by
      have h_diff : Measurable
          (fun ω : Ω => chi₂ ω - chi_tilde (s.m ω)) :=
        h_chi₂_meas.sub (h_chi_tilde_meas.comp s.m_measurable)
      have h_set_eq : {ω : Ω | chi₂ ω = chi_tilde (s.m ω)}
          = (fun ω : Ω => chi₂ ω - chi_tilde (s.m ω)) ⁻¹' ({0} : Set _) := by
        ext ω; simp [sub_eq_zero]
      rw [h_set_eq]
      exact h_diff (measurableSet_singleton 0)
    have h_chi₁_eq_prior : ∀ᵐ ω ∂s.prior.toMeasure,
        chi₁ ω = chi_tilde (s.m ω) := by
      have h_pulled := (MeasureTheory.ae_map_iff measurable_snd.aemeasurable
        h_meas_pred₁).mpr h_chi₁_eq_pi
      rw [h_marg₁_snd] at h_pulled
      exact h_pulled
    have h_chi₂_eq_prior : ∀ᵐ ω ∂s.prior.toMeasure,
        chi₂ ω = chi_tilde (s.m ω) := by
      have h_pulled := (MeasureTheory.ae_map_iff measurable_snd.aemeasurable
        h_meas_pred₂).mpr h_chi₂_eq_pi
      rw [h_marg₂_snd] at h_pulled
      exact h_pulled
    filter_upwards [h_chi₁_eq_prior, h_chi₂_eq_prior] with ω h₁ h₂
    exact h₁.trans h₂.symm
  apply MeasureTheory.ProbabilityMeasure.toMeasure_injective
  rw [h_pi₁_eq, h_pi₂_eq]
  apply MeasureTheory.Measure.map_congr
  filter_upwards [h_chi_eq] with ω hω
  rw [hω]

/-- **Uniqueness and the Bayes-plausible selector.**

The moment-persuasion problem admits a unique optimal joint `pi*`.  Its active set `S` satisfies
`S ⊆ S_star v S`, and `pi*` is generated by a Bayes-plausible selector: There is a measurable
cell-assignment `χ : Ω → X` into `S` (a `BayesPlausibleSelector s S`) such that condition (M)
holds.

The full hypothesis list, all explicit below: Lipschitzness of the moment coordinates (`hm_lip`);
Lipschitzness, `C¹`-smoothness, measurability, boundedness, and upper semicontinuity of `v`
(`hv_lip`, `hv_diff`, `hv_meas`, `hv_bdd`, `hv_usc`); measurability and upper semicontinuity of the
composed value (`hV_meas`, `hV_usc`); Lipschitzness of the posterior check of every Lipschitz price
on `X` (`h_pcheck_lip`); an open-positive prior measure (`IsOpenPosMeasure`); density of the moment
image in `X` (`h_dense`); and the genericity and absolute-continuity conditions of
`MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable` (`hDiff`).  The `MomentSetup` surjectivity field `moment_surjOn_X`
(every point of `X` is achievable as a posterior moment) is in force as part of `s`.

In the classical interval setting `Ω = X` the selector's cells `χ⁻¹({x})` are convex (the optimum
is convex-partitional); that convexity is not expressible under the present abstract hypotheses on
`Ω` and is not asserted here. -/
theorem unique_optimal_joint_bayesPlausible
    (s : MomentSetup Ω n) (hm_lip : s.IsCoordLipschitz)
    {v : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ} {L : NNReal}
    (hv_lip : LipschitzWith L (fun x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) => v x))
    (hv_diff : ContDiff ℝ 1 v)
    (hv_meas : Measurable v) (hv_bdd : ∃ M, ∀ x, |v x| ≤ M)
    (hv_usc : UpperSemicontinuous v)
    (hV_meas : Measurable (s.composedValue v))
    (hV_usc : UpperSemicontinuous (s.composedValue v))
    (h_pcheck_lip : ∀ {p : Ω → ℝ} {K : NNReal},
      LipschitzWith K p → LipschitzOnWith K (convexRoof s p) s.X)
    [s.prior.toMeasure.IsOpenPosMeasure]
    (h_dense : s.X ⊆ closure (Set.range s.m))
    (hDiff : MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable s v) :
    ∃! pi ∈ feasibleJoint s,
      (∫ p, v p.1 ∂pi.toMeasure = momentPrimal s v) ∧
      ∃ (S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (_ : BayesPlausibleSelector s S),
        S ⊆ S_star s v S ∧ ConditionM s v pi S := by
  have hV_bdd : ∃ M, ∀ μ : ProbDist Ω, |s.composedValue v μ| ≤ M := by
    obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := hv_bdd
    exact ⟨M, fun μ => hM (s.posteriorMoment μ)⟩
  obtain ⟨pi_star, hpi_feas, hpi_val⟩ :=
    exists_optimal_joint s hm_lip hv_lip hv_meas hv_bdd hv_usc hV_bdd hV_usc
  obtain ⟨S, hM, hS_sub⟩ :=
    (optimality_iff_M_with_Sstar s hm_lip hv_lip hv_diff hv_meas hv_bdd hv_usc
        hV_meas hV_usc h_pcheck_lip pi_star hpi_feas h_dense).mp hpi_val
  obtain ⟨hCP⟩ := exists_bayesPlausibleSelector_of_optimal_joint s hv_lip hv_diff hDiff pi_star
    S hM hS_sub
  refine ⟨pi_star, ⟨hpi_feas, hpi_val, S, hCP, hS_sub, hM⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro pi' ⟨hpi'_feas, hpi'_val, _⟩
  exact MomentSetup.IsDifferentiable.unique_optimal_joint s hm_lip hv_lip hv_diff hv_meas hv_bdd
    hv_usc hV_meas hV_usc h_pcheck_lip h_dense hDiff
    pi' pi_star hpi'_feas hpi_feas hpi'_val hpi_val

end Econlib.MechanismDesign.InformationDesign.Persuasion.Moment
